WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.099 --> 00:00:04.766
(angelic music)

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:14.330
- From no French model,
breathes the muse tonight

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.000
the scene she draws is horrid, not polite.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.828
She dips her pen in
terror, will ye shrink?

00:00:22.828 --> 00:00:26.499
Shall foreign critics
teach you how to think?

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:30.170
Had Shakespeare's magic
dignified the stage?

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.620
If timid laws had
schooled the insipid age?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.360
Had Hamlet's specter
trod the midnight round?

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.513
Or Banquo's issue been in vision crowned?

00:00:42.722 --> 00:00:47.350
Free as your country,
Britons, be your scene.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.933
Be nature now, and now invention queen.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:56.326
Be vice alone corrected and restrained.

00:00:56.326 --> 00:01:00.240
Can crimes be punished
by a bard enchained?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.900
Shall the bold censor
back be sent to school,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.832
and told, "This is not
nice, that is not rule."

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:10.670
The French no crimes of magnitude admit.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.402
They seldom startle, just alarm the pit.

00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:20.402
The tragic Greeks, with
nobler license wrote

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.209
nor veiled the eye, but
plucked away the mote.

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:29.737
Whatever passion prompted, was their game

00:01:29.737 --> 00:01:34.314
not delicate, while
chastisement their aim.

00:01:34.314 --> 00:01:38.931
Electra now a parent's blood demands.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:43.931
Now parricide distains the Theban's hands.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:49.010
And love incestuous
knots his nuptial bands.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.710
Such is our scene, from real life it rose.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.260
Tremendous picture of domestic woes.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:03.340
If terror shake you, or soft pity move,

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.081
if dreadful pangs o'ertake unbridled love.

00:02:07.081 --> 00:02:12.081
Excuse the bard, who
from your feeling draws

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:17.123
all the reward he aims at, your applause.

00:02:17.997 --> 00:02:20.247
(applause)

00:02:42.118 --> 00:02:44.785
(angelic music)

00:03:04.931 --> 00:03:07.764
(thunder roaring)

00:03:18.524 --> 00:03:20.970
- What awful silence!

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.540
How these antique towers and vacant courts

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.730
dull the suspended soul,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.590
till expectation wears the cast of fear

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.160
and fear half-ready to become devotion,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.193
mumbles a kind of mental orison.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.214
I met a peasant, and inquired my way.

00:03:39.214 --> 00:03:42.520
The churl, not rude of speech,

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.450
but like the tenant of
some night-haunted ruin,

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.305
bore an aspect of
horror, worn to habitude.

00:03:48.305 --> 00:03:52.220
None there, said he, are welcome,

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.626
but now and then a pious
mass-priest, and the poor,

00:03:55.626 --> 00:03:59.260
to whom the Countess deals
her alms on covenant,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.200
that each revolving night
they beg of heaven the health

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.443
of her son's soul and her own.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000
What precious mummery!

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.850
Her son in exile,

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.020
she wastes on monks and
beggars his inheritance,

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.733
for his soul's health!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.140
I never knew a woman but loved our bodies

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.233
or our souls too well.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:28.540
- Methought I heard a stranger's voice.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.080
What lack you, sir?

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.570
- Good fellow, who inhabits here?

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:33.935
- I do.

00:04:33.935 --> 00:04:36.885
- Belike this castle is not thine.

00:04:36.885 --> 00:04:37.885
- Belike so,

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.447
but be it whose it may,

00:04:40.447 --> 00:04:43.880
this is no haunt For revellers
and gallants, pass your way.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.300
- Thou churl!

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.421
Is this your Gallic hospitality?

00:04:47.421 --> 00:04:49.460
Thy lady, on my life,

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.224
would not thus rudely
chide from her presence

00:04:52.224 --> 00:04:53.880
a bewildered knight.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.253
- Angels defend us!

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:57.161
What a reprobate!

00:04:57.161 --> 00:04:59.480
Thou know'st my lady then!

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.170
Thou know'st her not.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:05.931
Canst thou in hair-cloths
vex those dainty limbs?

00:05:05.931 --> 00:05:09.159
Canst thou on reeking
pavements and cold marble,

00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:13.240
in meditation pass the live-long night?

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.372
- Father grey-beard, I cry you mercy.

00:05:15.372 --> 00:05:18.590
- Time was, my lord,

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:22.871
the Count of Narbonne,
a prosperous gentleman.

00:05:22.871 --> 00:05:27.871
Were he alive, we should not
know these moping melancholies.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:30.957
Heaven rest his soul!

00:05:30.957 --> 00:05:35.120
I marvel not my lady
cherishes his remembrance,

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.460
for he was comely to sight,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.560
and wondrous goodly built.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.560
They say, his son Count Edmund's

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.467
mainly like him.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.650
- What if I bring tidings of Count Edmund?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.480
- Last night the raven croak'd,

00:05:56.497 --> 00:06:00.264
and from the bars of our
lodge-fire flitted a messenger.

00:06:00.264 --> 00:06:03.120
I knew no good would follow.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:07.100
Oh, no, no, he must not here alas!

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.233
I prithee, he must not here set foot.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.840
Does my old master's heir
still breathe this vital air?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.023
Is he in France?

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:23.670
I would make a weary pilgrimage

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.298
to kiss his gracious hands,

00:06:26.298 --> 00:06:31.090
and at his feet lay my old bones.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.560
- But say, why Narbonne's heir

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.900
from Narbonne's lands is banished

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.700
driven by a ruthless mother?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:42.700
- Ah sir, 'tis hard indeed,
but spare his mother.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:48.680
Such virtue never dwelt in female form.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.320
But so,

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:54.960
count Edmund being not
sixteen, a lusty youth,

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.550
his father's very image.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:01.763
I come to the point,
her name was Beatrice.

00:07:04.003 --> 00:07:05.086
Aye, Beatrice

00:07:07.117 --> 00:07:10.002
a rogueish eye, she
never would look at me.

00:07:10.002 --> 00:07:11.085
This Beatrice

00:07:13.227 --> 00:07:14.060
but hark!

00:07:16.422 --> 00:07:17.589
My lady comes.

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:21.970
Retire a while beyond the yews,

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.970
anon I'll tell you more.

00:07:26.143 --> 00:07:28.810
(angelic music)

00:08:13.765 --> 00:08:15.015
'Tis ever thus.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:20.510
At break of morn, she
hies to yonder abbey,

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:23.756
and prostate o'er some monumental stone,

00:08:23.756 --> 00:08:28.183
seems more to wait her
doom, than ask to shun it.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.065
But hush.

00:08:31.065 --> 00:08:33.315
Who moves up yonder avenue?

00:08:34.317 --> 00:08:36.730
It is he, Benedict,

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:40.130
my lady's confessor, with Friar Martin.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.840
Quick hide thee hence,

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.982
should that same meddling
monk observe our conference,

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:47.570
there were fine work toward.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:50.630
Loiter about yon grange,
I come to thee there.

00:08:52.323 --> 00:08:55.073
(chorus singing)

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.250
- Ay!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.320
Sift her, sift her I tell thee, brother,

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.774
this woman was not cast in human mould.

00:09:17.774 --> 00:09:21.090
Ten such would foil a council,

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.457
would unbuild our Roman church

00:09:23.457 --> 00:09:26.130
in her, devotion's real.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:31.010
She prays because she feels,
and feels, because a sinner.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:34.320
- What is this secret
sin, this untold tale,

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.050
that art cannot extract,
nor penance cleanse?

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:43.050
Loss of a husband, sixteen
years enjoyed and dead as many

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.980
could not stamp such sorrow.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.590
- My mind has more than once imputed blood

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:50.600
to this incessant mourner.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:54.730
Beatrice, the damsel
for whose sake in exile

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.479
she holds her only son, has never,

00:09:57.479 --> 00:10:02.479
since the night of his
incontinence, been seen or heard of.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.030
- 'Tis clear, 'tis clear!

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:08.030
- I have oft shifted
my discourse to murder.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.310
She notes it not.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.542
Her muscles hold their place

00:10:11.542 --> 00:10:14.819
no sudden flushing, no faltering lip.

00:10:14.819 --> 00:10:16.497
I've fixed on love,

00:10:16.497 --> 00:10:18.210
The failure of the sex,

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.717
and aptest cause of each attendant crime.

00:10:20.717 --> 00:10:25.310
- Aye, brother, there we
master all their craft.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:28.070
- Still, brother, do you err?

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:31.600
The Count Her husband,
so adored and so lamented

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.440
won not her fancy,

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:37.510
till the nuptial rites had
with the sting of pleasure

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:38.620
taught her passion.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.773
- Then whither turn to
worm her secret out?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.770
- I know not that, nay.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.041
One unguarded moment may
disclose this mystic tale

00:10:47.041 --> 00:10:49.590
then, brother, what a harvest.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:54.061
Or soon, or late, a praying
woman must become our spoil.

00:10:54.061 --> 00:10:55.930
- Her zeal may falter.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.020
- I nurse her in new horrors,

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:01.440
form her tenants to
fancy visions, phantoms,

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.810
and report them.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.497
She mocks their fond
credulity, but trust me,

00:11:05.497 --> 00:11:08.440
her memory retains their colouring.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:10.003
- This is masterly.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.317
- Oh, were I seated high as my ambition

00:11:15.317 --> 00:11:18.383
I'd place this naked foot
on necks of monarchs.

00:11:19.795 --> 00:11:24.130
- By humbler arts our humble fabric rose.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.000
Win power by craft,

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.340
wear it with ostentation.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:32.800
Gain to the Holy See this fair
domain and a crimson bonnet

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.525
may reward your toils.

00:11:34.525 --> 00:11:36.597
- Never, while Edmund lives.

00:11:36.597 --> 00:11:40.870
This steady woman can ne'er
be pious with so many virtues.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:44.060
Justice is interwoven in her frame.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:47.220
Nor will she wrong the
son she will not see.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.850
She loves him not,

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.460
yet is mistress of his fortunes
usurp'd from her own wants,

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.970
she sets apart a scanty
portion only for her ward,

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:56.350
Young Adeliza.

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.310
- 'Twere wise to school this maiden,

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:01.920
lead the train of young
ideas to a fancied object.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:04.900
A mental spouse.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.830
- This is already done.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.569
But Edmund's death were hopes more solid.

00:12:09.569 --> 00:12:13.320
- First report him dead.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.793
His letters intercepted.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.103
- Greatly thought.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.830
Lo, where comes our patroness, leave me

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.230
- Alas!

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.960
Must guilt ground our very virtues?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.513
Grow they on sin alone, and not on grace?

00:12:38.364 --> 00:12:40.589
While Narbonne lived,

00:12:40.589 --> 00:12:44.760
my fully-sated soul thought none unhappy

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.280
for it did not think!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.550
Well!

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:49.556
Peace is fled,

00:12:49.556 --> 00:12:51.316
ne'er to return!

00:12:51.316 --> 00:12:55.130
Nor dare I snap the thread of life.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:58.700
Eternity has scope enough to punish me,

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.620
tho' I should borrow a few short hours

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.510
to sacrifice to charity.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.155
- I sought you, lady.

00:13:05.155 --> 00:13:07.180
- Happily I'm found.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.730
Who needs the widow's mite?

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:10.729
- None asks your aid.

00:13:10.729 --> 00:13:15.290
Your gracious foresight
still prevents occasion.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.440
- No more of this, good father.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.675
I suspect none of your
holy order of dissembling.

00:13:20.675 --> 00:13:23.410
Suspect not me of loving flattery.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:25.120
Will it give me virtues?

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.260
- The church could seal your
pardon, but you scorn it.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:33.520
Yours are Pagan virtues,
as such I praise them,

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.280
but as such condemn them.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:38.600
- Father, my crimes are Pagan.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:41.322
Why shakes my soul with nightly terrors?

00:13:41.322 --> 00:13:43.783
'Tis from within I tremble.

00:13:43.783 --> 00:13:45.450
Death would be felicity.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.540
What joys have I?

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.970
I have lost my husband.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.930
My own decree has banished my own son.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:57.220
- Last night I dreamt your
son was with the blessed.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.124
- Would heaven he were!

00:13:59.124 --> 00:14:01.840
- Do you then wish his death?

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.505
- Should I not wish him blest?

00:14:04.505 --> 00:14:07.470
- Madam, I must not hear this language.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:09.790
You do abuse my patience.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.630
It ill beseems my holy
function to give countenance

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:17.820
by lending ear to such pernicious tenets.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.114
I am wrapt beyond my bearing!

00:14:21.114 --> 00:14:23.300
Your son is dead!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:27.850
- Father, we no prophetic demon bear

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:30.053
within our breast but conscience.

00:14:30.053 --> 00:14:31.903
That has spoken.

00:14:31.903 --> 00:14:34.170
'Tis that voice has told me,

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:37.450
'twas my son's birth, not his mortality,

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:39.900
must drown my soul in woe.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.269
- Unjust, uncharitable as your words,

00:14:43.269 --> 00:14:44.800
I pardon them.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:45.633
- Forgive me, Father.

00:14:45.633 --> 00:14:48.040
Discretion does not guide my words.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.149
What peace is there for me!

00:14:50.149 --> 00:14:52.380
- In the neighboring district

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:53.880
where lives a holy man,

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:56.667
whose sanctity is marked
with wondrous gifts.

00:14:56.667 --> 00:14:58.280
Consult with him.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.130
- Consult a holy man?

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.570
Inquire of him?

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:03.650
Good father, wherefore?

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.104
What should I inquire?

00:15:05.104 --> 00:15:08.800
Must I be taught of him, that sin is woe?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.000
Must I learn that minutes
stamped with crimes

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.680
are past recall?

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.653
That joys are momentary,
and remorse Eternal?

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.470
Death alone can certify whether,

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:24.267
when justice's full dues exacted,

00:15:24.267 --> 00:15:29.267
mercy shall grant one
drop to slake my torment.

00:15:29.806 --> 00:15:32.275
Here, father, break off.

00:15:32.275 --> 00:15:34.393
You to your calling,

00:15:34.393 --> 00:15:38.483
I to my tears and mournful occupation.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:46.900
- Doubt not my friend.

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:50.427
Hardships of war have chased
out the bloom of comeliness

00:15:50.427 --> 00:15:53.660
and stamped this face
with harsher lineaments

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:57.076
that well may mock the
prying of a mothers eye.

00:15:57.076 --> 00:15:59.840
A mother, through whose firm nerves

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:03.220
tumultuous instinct's flood
ne'er gushed to tell her,

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.380
this is your son!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.730
- If not her love, my
lord, suspect her hatred.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.590
Hatred is distempered love.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:11.093
- Why should she hate me?

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:15.167
For that my opening
passion's swelling ardour

00:16:15.167 --> 00:16:18.960
prompted a congenial necessary joy,

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.223
was that a cause?

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:24.890
No, Florian, she herself was woman then,

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.070
A sensual woman.

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:30.060
She might have pardoned
what she felt so well.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:33.010
- Forgive me, Edmund, nor think I preach.

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.682
You have often told me that night,

00:16:34.682 --> 00:16:37.130
the very night that to your arms

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:40.710
gave pretty Beatrice's melting beauties,

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.226
was the same night on
which your father died.

00:16:43.226 --> 00:16:44.823
- 'Tis true.

00:16:46.038 --> 00:16:50.456
Wouldst thou have turned
thee from a willing girl,

00:16:50.456 --> 00:16:53.603
to sing a requiem to thy father's soul?

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:58.340
I thought my mother busied with her tears

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.350
while I stole to Beatrice's chamber.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.750
How my mother became apprized I know not,

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.920
but her heart grew estranged, estranged!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.804
- 'Twas the trick of over-acted sorrow.

00:17:06.804 --> 00:17:08.330
Grief fatigues.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.290
- Still must I doubt,
still deem some mystery

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.710
beyond a widow's pious artifice.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:17.430
But, to me her hand is
bounteous as her heart is cold.

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:19.320
Narbonne's revenues are as fully mine

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.380
as if I held them by the
strength of charters.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:23.565
- Why set them on the hazard then?

00:17:23.565 --> 00:17:26.810
- I am weary, Florian,

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.145
of such a vagrant life.

00:17:29.145 --> 00:17:31.260
Befits it me,

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:35.160
sprung from a race of
heroes, Narbonne's prince,

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.590
to lend my causal arm's approved valour

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.820
to quarrels, nor my country's nor my own?

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.460
I fought at Buda 'gainst the Turk,

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.690
a holy war, so was it deemed.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.629
I smote the turban'd race.

00:17:47.629 --> 00:17:51.400
Mattered it to me whether
crescent or cross prevailed?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.300
- True, my lord.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.400
Deadly feuds for obsolete offences.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:58.530
- Thy reproof my friend, is just.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:02.563
But had I not cause a tender
cause, that prompted my return?

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.523
This cruel parent, whom
I blame, and mourn,

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.730
has won my love, by winning my respect.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.562
She cannot surely, after such perils,

00:18:14.562 --> 00:18:17.420
wounds by her command encountered,

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:21.783
after sixteen exiled years,
spurn me when kneeling.

00:18:24.565 --> 00:18:26.033
Thinkst thou 'tis possible?

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.860
- I would not think it,

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.360
but a host of priests surround her.

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:34.490
They, good men, are seldom found

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:36.830
to please the cause of pity.

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:38.440
You shall be beggared,

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.852
that the saint your mother may

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:43.330
by cowl'd sychophants
and canting jugglers,

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:45.503
be hailed a new Teresa.

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.670
Pray be not seen here.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:51.050
Let's again to the wars.

00:18:51.050 --> 00:18:53.020
- No, Florian.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.331
My dulled soul is sick of riot,

00:18:55.331 --> 00:18:58.940
'tis time to bid adieu to vagrant pleasure

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:01.000
and fix the wanderer love.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.190
Domestic bliss.

00:19:02.190 --> 00:19:06.520
- Ah, yes, your fair pensioner,

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:10.710
young Adeliza, has
sobered your inconstancy.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.570
Tell me is she must be fruitful.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:14.200
- Pass we this levity.

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:18.260
'Tis true, Adeliza is
beauty's type renewed.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.283
- Is she kind?

00:19:19.283 --> 00:19:22.623
- Cold as the metal bars
that part her from me.

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.798
- How gain'd you then admittance?

00:19:25.798 --> 00:19:27.650
- This whole month,

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.170
while waiting your arrival,

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.323
I have haunted her convent's parlour.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:35.090
O Florian, union with that favoured maiden

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.944
might reconcile my mother.

00:19:36.944 --> 00:19:39.540
Hark, I hear voices that seem approaching.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.790
They cannot know me, see!

00:19:48.017 --> 00:19:50.934
(children singing)

00:19:58.427 --> 00:20:00.640
Sweet Children, in whose behalf raises

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:04.000
these little suppliants their
artless hands to heaven?

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.130
- You seem a stranger,

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:07.500
or you could but know, sir knight,

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.440
that Narbonne's pious
Countess dwells within,

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.540
A lady most disconsolate.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:17.075
Her lord was snatched away
in lusty life's full vantage,

00:20:17.075 --> 00:20:18.770
but no account made up!

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.770
No absolution!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.610
Hence, his weeping relict
o'eer his spot of doom

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.170
a goodly cross erected.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:28.870
Thither we proceed to
chaunt our holy dirge,

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.514
and offer due intercession
for his soul's repose.

00:20:32.514 --> 00:20:34.910
- I knew his son.

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:35.810
- Edmund?

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:37.660
Where sojourns he?

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.400
- In the grave.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.940
- Is Edmund dead?

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:41.773
Say how.

00:20:41.773 --> 00:20:43.390
- He fell at Budapest.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.100
And not to his dishonour.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:48.160
- Sixteen fatal years has
Narbonne's province groaned

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:50.283
beneath the hand of desolation.

00:20:50.283 --> 00:20:52.524
For what crimes we know not!

00:20:52.524 --> 00:20:54.841
- I feel your country's woes.

00:20:54.841 --> 00:20:57.963
I loved Edmund, revered
his father's ashes.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:01.630
I will visit this ruined monument

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:05.010
and at our leisure could with
some conference with you.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.090
- This is well.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.350
Where is your haunt?

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:09.670
- A mile without the town

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:11.410
hard by St. Bridget's nunnery.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:14.243
- There expect me I must to Benedict.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.747
(thunder roaring)

00:21:20.747 --> 00:21:22.997
- Return, my gracious lady.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:28.451
Though the storm abates his
clamours, do not go forth.

00:21:28.451 --> 00:21:31.550
I saw the lightning burst on the monument.

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:35.160
The shield of Narbonne's
arms shivered to splinters,

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:37.270
down with hideous crash,

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:39.300
the cross came tumbling.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:40.940
Then I fled, hark!

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.500
Sure I heard a groan!

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.770
- Wretches like me, good
Peter, dread no storms.

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:48.370
'Tis my soul's proper language.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:53.370
Behold she comes a voluntary victim.

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:54.920
Shade of my Narbonne

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.810
accept her destined head.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:58.980
- Oh for pity!

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:01.960
Gracious dame, what words are these?

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.614
In any mouth less holy they
would seem a magic incantation.

00:22:05.614 --> 00:22:08.670
Last year's eclipse fell out

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:11.470
because your maidens
crossed a gypsy's palm

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.654
to know what was become of Beatrice.

00:22:13.654 --> 00:22:17.904
Who knows, but sudden
malady took off the damsel?

00:22:17.904 --> 00:22:19.827
Beatrice might, or might not,

00:22:19.827 --> 00:22:23.110
have sepulture within the castle walls.

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:23.943
- Peace fool.

00:22:23.943 --> 00:22:27.610
Thy equivocation has stained my name

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:29.660
with murder's foul suspicion!

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:34.033
Things foreign rise and load
me with their blackness.

00:22:34.996 --> 00:22:38.210
Erroneous imputation must be borne,

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:41.360
lest, while unravelling the knotty web,

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:45.476
I lend a clue may vibrate to my heart.

00:22:45.476 --> 00:22:47.233
But who comes here?

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:49.053
Retire.

00:22:51.263 --> 00:22:53.810
- 'Tis not far off the time the porter

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:55.786
willed me to expect him here.

00:22:55.786 --> 00:22:58.361
Oh, Edmund, may my prosperous care

00:22:58.361 --> 00:23:01.490
restore thee to thy state.

00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:04.023
And aid thy love for Adeliza.

00:23:04.023 --> 00:23:06.141
- [Countess] Methought he
spoke of love and Adeliza!

00:23:06.141 --> 00:23:07.097
Who can it be?

00:23:07.097 --> 00:23:09.350
[Porter] I never heard his name

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:10.641
- Stranger,

00:23:10.641 --> 00:23:15.641
did chance or purpose guide thy steps

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:18.150
to this lone dwelling?

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:20.656
- Pardon, gentle lady.

00:23:20.656 --> 00:23:23.890
If curious to behold the pious matron

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:25.803
whom Narbonne's plains obey,

00:23:25.803 --> 00:23:27.850
I sought this castle.

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:29.830
- Me, stranger.

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:32.136
Is affliction then so rare?

00:23:32.136 --> 00:23:37.136
None dwell here but melancholy,
sorrow, and contrition.

00:23:37.603 --> 00:23:42.603
- Pleasure has charms,
but so has virtue too.

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.340
- Your courtly phrase, young knight,

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:46.700
bespeaks a birth above the vulgar.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:49.193
- [Porter] Lady, 'tis the hour of prayer.

00:23:50.512 --> 00:23:53.513
- Stranger, I'm summoned hence.

00:23:53.513 --> 00:23:56.946
At St. Bridget's monastery tomorrow night,

00:23:56.946 --> 00:24:00.830
if you can spare some
moments from your pastime,

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:04.213
I would talk with thee in
presence of the abbess.

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:12.681
- So, this is well, my introduction made.

00:24:12.681 --> 00:24:15.262
It follows that I move her for her son.

00:24:15.262 --> 00:24:19.237
Women often wear the mask
of piety to draw respect,

00:24:19.237 --> 00:24:21.820
or hide the loss of it.

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:24.280
While snuffing incense,
and devoutly wanton,

00:24:24.280 --> 00:24:27.441
the Pagan goddess grows a Christian saint.

00:24:27.441 --> 00:24:28.843
Well!

00:24:28.843 --> 00:24:31.403
Edmund, whatso'er thy mother be,

00:24:31.403 --> 00:24:35.990
I'll put her virtue or
hypocrisy to the severest tests.

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:38.792
Countess, expect me!

00:24:38.792 --> 00:24:41.625
(thunder roaring)

00:24:48.499 --> 00:24:51.249
(mournful music)

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:10.690
- The monument destroyed

00:25:11.862 --> 00:25:14.460
Well, what of that!

00:25:14.460 --> 00:25:16.490
Were every thunderbolt addressed to me,

00:25:16.490 --> 00:25:18.530
no one would miss me.

00:25:18.530 --> 00:25:20.380
We know the doom we merit.

00:25:20.380 --> 00:25:21.213
Fie, fie!

00:25:23.400 --> 00:25:26.238
I blush to recollect my weakness.

00:25:26.238 --> 00:25:28.852
My Edmund may be dead,

00:25:28.852 --> 00:25:33.227
my Adeliza may taste the cup
of woe that I have drugged.

00:25:33.227 --> 00:25:37.050
What wretch could be a
blacker criminal than I am?

00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:40.480
Were faggots placed around me
and the fatal torch applied

00:25:40.480 --> 00:25:43.820
would it teach the world unheard of sins?

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:46.380
How dare I be esteemed?

00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:48.963
Be known my crimes!

00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:50.833
My Edmund!

00:25:51.740 --> 00:25:54.893
Has not a mother's hand
afflicted him enough?

00:25:58.240 --> 00:26:01.888
- Madam, young Adeliza
intreats to speak with you.

00:26:01.888 --> 00:26:05.412
The lady abbess sickens to death.

00:26:05.412 --> 00:26:06.333
- Admit her.

00:26:07.420 --> 00:26:10.003
Now my soul recall thy calm.

00:26:12.470 --> 00:26:14.609
Approach, sweet maid.

00:26:14.609 --> 00:26:17.740
Thy melancholy mein
speaks thy compassionate

00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:18.950
and feeling heart.

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:21.530
- Oh, Can I hear this praise,

00:26:21.530 --> 00:26:24.370
and not fall in blushes at thy feet?

00:26:24.370 --> 00:26:27.616
Recall thy words thy
Adeliza merits no encomium.

00:26:27.616 --> 00:26:29.662
I am not innocent!

00:26:29.662 --> 00:26:34.258
- Thou dearest orphan to my bosom come.

00:26:34.258 --> 00:26:38.573
Purity like thine affrights
itself with fancied guilt.

00:26:38.573 --> 00:26:40.499
- In vain you cheer me.

00:26:40.499 --> 00:26:42.740
I am most unworthy.

00:26:42.740 --> 00:26:45.484
Other discourse than thine
has charmed mine ear,

00:26:45.484 --> 00:26:48.010
nor dare I now presume
to call thee mother.

00:26:48.010 --> 00:26:52.726
- My lovely innocence, restrain thy tears.

00:26:52.726 --> 00:26:55.003
I know thy secret.

00:26:55.950 --> 00:26:58.820
Know, why beats and
throbs thy little heart

00:26:58.820 --> 00:27:00.200
with unaccustomed tumult.

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:01.440
- Impossible!

00:27:01.440 --> 00:27:02.994
- I will tell it thee.

00:27:02.994 --> 00:27:05.910
Thou hast conversed with a young knight.

00:27:05.910 --> 00:27:06.890
- Amazement!

00:27:06.890 --> 00:27:08.780
Who informed thee?

00:27:08.780 --> 00:27:10.820
Pent in her chamber, sickness has detained

00:27:10.820 --> 00:27:12.289
our abbess from the parlour.

00:27:12.289 --> 00:27:15.810
There I saw him of as he came alone.

00:27:15.810 --> 00:27:17.710
- He talked of love?

00:27:17.710 --> 00:27:18.770
- He did.

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:22.670
- 'Tis well, this is the
stranger I beheld this morning.

00:27:22.670 --> 00:27:25.090
- He sorrows for a father.

00:27:25.090 --> 00:27:28.680
Something too he uttered
of a large inheritance

00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:29.690
that should be his.

00:27:29.690 --> 00:27:32.360
- Dost thou love this stranger?

00:27:32.360 --> 00:27:35.503
- Yes, with such love
as that I feel for thee.

00:27:36.370 --> 00:27:38.810
His earnest words sound like the precepts

00:27:38.810 --> 00:27:40.250
of a tender parent.

00:27:40.250 --> 00:27:43.720
And next to thee, I
think I could obey him.

00:27:43.720 --> 00:27:46.320
- Be calm, my lovely orphan!

00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:47.582
Hush thy fears.

00:27:47.582 --> 00:27:51.600
Heaven knows how fondly,
anxiously, I love thee!

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:54.310
The stranger's not to blame.

00:27:54.310 --> 00:27:57.730
Myself will task him, and
see if he deserves thee.

00:27:57.730 --> 00:28:01.873
Now retire, nor slack thy
duty to the expiring saint.

00:28:04.763 --> 00:28:07.513
(chorus singing)

00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:19.030
- The dew of grace rest on this dwelling.

00:28:19.030 --> 00:28:22.140
- Thanks, my ghostly friend.

00:28:22.140 --> 00:28:25.270
- Or I mistake, in your sad eye,

00:28:25.270 --> 00:28:28.070
I spell affliction's signature.

00:28:28.070 --> 00:28:30.977
- To tutor my unapt and
ill-schooled nature,

00:28:30.977 --> 00:28:33.493
you come then, with
doctrines and authority.

00:28:33.493 --> 00:28:37.380
If ought can medicate
a soul unsound as mine.

00:28:37.380 --> 00:28:41.950
- You mock my friendship,
and miscall my zeal.

00:28:41.950 --> 00:28:44.010
Learn the measure of your woes.

00:28:44.010 --> 00:28:47.075
Learn, if the mother's fortitude

00:28:47.075 --> 00:28:51.420
can brave the bolt the
woman's arrogance defied.

00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:53.320
- The mother, said'st thou?

00:28:53.320 --> 00:28:55.380
- Yes, imperious dame.

00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:58.244
On Buda's plain thy
slaughtered Edmund lies.

00:28:58.244 --> 00:29:01.080
An unbeliever's weapon cleft his heart.

00:29:01.080 --> 00:29:05.294
- In the grave, thou
sayest, my Edmund sleeps.

00:29:05.294 --> 00:29:07.839
How didst thou learn his fate?

00:29:07.839 --> 00:29:09.633
Priest, mock me not!

00:29:09.633 --> 00:29:11.238
- Then you loved him?

00:29:11.238 --> 00:29:12.763
- Loved him!

00:29:12.763 --> 00:29:15.693
Oh, nature, bleeding at my heart,

00:29:15.693 --> 00:29:17.150
hearest thou this?

00:29:17.150 --> 00:29:18.760
Loved him?

00:29:18.760 --> 00:29:19.593
Ha!

00:29:19.593 --> 00:29:22.120
I am thy mistress yet,

00:29:22.120 --> 00:29:24.660
nor will I brook insolent reproof.

00:29:24.660 --> 00:29:28.290
Produce thy warrant,
assure my Edmund's death

00:29:28.290 --> 00:29:30.650
or dread his vengeance!

00:29:30.650 --> 00:29:32.890
- My warrant is at hand.

00:29:32.890 --> 00:29:35.220
This gentleman beheld thy Edmund

00:29:35.220 --> 00:29:36.993
breathless on the ground.

00:29:39.153 --> 00:29:41.592
- Hah, Is this sorcery?

00:29:41.592 --> 00:29:43.009
Or is my husband?

00:29:44.461 --> 00:29:45.623
(laughter)

00:29:45.623 --> 00:29:47.682
- Look up, o ever dear!

00:29:47.682 --> 00:29:51.200
Behold thy son, it is thy Edmund's voice.

00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:52.410
Dumb still!

00:29:52.410 --> 00:29:53.720
I have killed her!

00:29:53.720 --> 00:29:54.760
My brain grows hot.

00:29:54.760 --> 00:29:57.010
- My lord, restrain your passion.

00:29:57.010 --> 00:29:58.883
See, She revives.

00:30:00.270 --> 00:30:01.893
- Art thou, or not, a mother?

00:30:03.280 --> 00:30:05.380
- Hah, who, where am I?

00:30:05.380 --> 00:30:07.086
Why did you hold me?

00:30:07.086 --> 00:30:09.480
Was it not my Narbonne?

00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:11.970
- Alas, she raves!

00:30:11.970 --> 00:30:13.920
- Hah, whom!

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:16.150
Quick, answer.

00:30:16.150 --> 00:30:18.647
Count of Narbonne, dost thou live?

00:30:18.647 --> 00:30:20.363
- Madam, behold your son.

00:30:21.300 --> 00:30:22.350
He kneels for pardon.

00:30:25.245 --> 00:30:27.320
- Distraction!

00:30:27.320 --> 00:30:30.861
What means this complicated
scene of horrors?

00:30:30.861 --> 00:30:34.210
Art thou my husband winged from other orbs

00:30:34.210 --> 00:30:35.623
to taunt my soul?

00:30:37.030 --> 00:30:38.880
What is this dubious form?

00:30:38.880 --> 00:30:41.000
Art thou my dead or my living son?

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.130
- I am thy living Edmund.

00:30:43.130 --> 00:30:45.480
Let these scalding tears
attest the existence

00:30:45.480 --> 00:30:46.460
of thy suffering son.

00:30:46.460 --> 00:30:48.288
- Ah, touch me not!

00:30:48.288 --> 00:30:49.899
- How?

00:30:49.899 --> 00:30:52.194
In that cruel breast revive then

00:30:52.194 --> 00:30:54.573
all sensations except affection?

00:30:56.650 --> 00:30:59.530
But now, thy eyes I seemed my father?

00:30:59.530 --> 00:31:02.630
At least for that
resemblance, sake embrace me.

00:31:02.630 --> 00:31:04.550
- Horror on horror!

00:31:04.550 --> 00:31:06.410
Blasted be thy tongue.

00:31:06.410 --> 00:31:09.060
- Lady, I doubt not your blessing

00:31:09.060 --> 00:31:11.980
first obtained and gracious pardon,

00:31:11.980 --> 00:31:13.820
he will obey your pleasure,

00:31:13.820 --> 00:31:17.080
and return to stranger climes.

00:31:17.080 --> 00:31:19.140
- 'Tis false.

00:31:19.140 --> 00:31:20.950
I will not hence.

00:31:20.950 --> 00:31:22.760
Am I not Narbonne's prince?

00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:23.650
Who will banish me?

00:31:23.650 --> 00:31:25.675
- Edmund, hear me!

00:31:25.675 --> 00:31:30.675
Thou art my son, and
I will prove a mother.

00:31:30.770 --> 00:31:33.410
But I am thy sovereign too.

00:31:33.410 --> 00:31:36.120
This state is mine.

00:31:36.120 --> 00:31:38.710
Benedict, attend me.

00:31:38.710 --> 00:31:42.343
Tomorrow, Edmund, shalt
thou learn my pleasure.

00:31:48.330 --> 00:31:50.123
- Why, this is majesty.

00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:52.893
Commanding sex!

00:31:53.730 --> 00:31:56.850
Strength, courage, all
our boasted attributes

00:31:56.850 --> 00:31:58.910
seems a borrowed ray,

00:31:58.910 --> 00:32:02.363
when virtue deigns to
speak with female organs.

00:32:03.730 --> 00:32:07.193
Yes, o my mother, I will learn to obey.

00:32:09.200 --> 00:32:12.090
Make but the blooming Adeliza mine,

00:32:12.090 --> 00:32:15.646
And bear, of me unquestioned,
Narbonne's scepter.

00:32:15.646 --> 00:32:20.023
'Till life's expiring lamp
resumes its wasted oil no more.

00:32:22.789 --> 00:32:25.539
(chorus singing)

00:32:47.320 --> 00:32:48.610
- I know thy spirit well.

00:32:48.610 --> 00:32:51.530
But 'till this hour I
have not seen thy passions

00:32:51.530 --> 00:32:53.240
boil o'er the bounds of prudence.

00:32:53.240 --> 00:32:54.433
- Mistake me not, good brother

00:32:54.433 --> 00:32:58.370
I would not know one half that I suspect

00:32:58.370 --> 00:33:02.145
'till I have acted as if not suspecting.

00:33:02.145 --> 00:33:04.372
'Tis time enough to make up our account,

00:33:04.372 --> 00:33:07.300
when we confess and kneel for absolution.

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:10.360
- Still does thy genius
soar above mankind!

00:33:10.360 --> 00:33:14.640
How many fathers of our holy
church in Benedict I view.

00:33:14.640 --> 00:33:16.473
- No flattery, brother

00:33:16.473 --> 00:33:20.180
'Tis true the church owes
Benedict some thanks.

00:33:20.180 --> 00:33:22.884
For her, I forgot I am a man.

00:33:22.884 --> 00:33:26.770
Enemies to roam our Benedict's foes.

00:33:26.770 --> 00:33:30.106
Interest bids us crush this
cockatrice and her egg.

00:33:30.106 --> 00:33:32.885
Already to those vagrants she inclines

00:33:32.885 --> 00:33:37.040
as if the rogues, that
preach reform to others,

00:33:37.040 --> 00:33:40.630
like idiots, minded to reform themselves.

00:33:40.630 --> 00:33:43.350
- Be cautious, brother,
you may lose the lady.

00:33:43.350 --> 00:33:45.250
- She is already lost.

00:33:45.250 --> 00:33:48.630
I cannot dupe, and
therefore must destroy her.

00:33:48.630 --> 00:33:50.380
- How may this be accomplished?

00:33:50.380 --> 00:33:52.240
- Ask me not.

00:33:52.240 --> 00:33:54.059
I guess her fatal secret.

00:33:54.059 --> 00:33:55.713
- I tremble!

00:33:57.360 --> 00:33:59.923
- Dastard, tremble if we fail.

00:34:04.533 --> 00:34:07.078
Peace, dotard, peace!

00:34:07.078 --> 00:34:10.516
Nor when the lamb is
nigh, must eagles wrangle.

00:34:10.516 --> 00:34:12.880
Why sighs that gentle bosom?

00:34:12.880 --> 00:34:17.083
- Ah, holy father, the
pious abbess is at peace.

00:34:17.083 --> 00:34:19.740
We go to bear her parting
blessing to the Countess.

00:34:19.740 --> 00:34:21.700
- It must not be by me.

00:34:21.700 --> 00:34:24.310
She wills you restrain your steps

00:34:24.310 --> 00:34:25.853
within the cloister's pale,

00:34:25.853 --> 00:34:29.484
nor grant access but
to one stranger knight.

00:34:29.484 --> 00:34:31.293
The Countess commands.

00:34:32.370 --> 00:34:33.563
- Hah, Adeliza!

00:34:34.410 --> 00:34:36.884
I charged thee guard thy convent.

00:34:36.884 --> 00:34:39.267
Wherefore then this disobedience?

00:34:39.267 --> 00:34:42.550
- Madam, I was urging the
fitness of your orders.

00:34:42.550 --> 00:34:45.420
- No, I am the thing you made me.

00:34:45.420 --> 00:34:47.958
Crush me, spurn me I will not murmur.

00:34:47.958 --> 00:34:51.980
Should you bid me die I know
'twere meant in kindness.

00:34:51.980 --> 00:34:53.692
- Bid thee die!

00:34:53.692 --> 00:34:58.234
My own detested life
but lingers round thee!

00:34:58.234 --> 00:35:02.931
My child, retire I am much discomposed.

00:35:02.931 --> 00:35:04.860
- Be patient lady.

00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:06.560
This fair domain, thou know'st,

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:08.930
acknowledges the
sovereignty of the church.

00:35:08.930 --> 00:35:10.129
Thy rebel son dres not attempt.

00:35:10.129 --> 00:35:12.485
- Again I bid thee peace.

00:35:12.485 --> 00:35:16.169
There is no question of Lord Edmund.

00:35:16.169 --> 00:35:17.413
Leave us,

00:35:18.620 --> 00:35:21.033
I have to talk with her alone.

00:35:22.810 --> 00:35:25.170
Now tremble at voices supernatural

00:35:25.170 --> 00:35:29.053
and forfeit the spoils the
tempest throws into our lap.

00:35:32.820 --> 00:35:33.653
Now,

00:35:35.488 --> 00:35:36.321
Adeliza,

00:35:37.720 --> 00:35:40.170
summon all thy courage,

00:35:40.170 --> 00:35:42.570
retrace my precepts past

00:35:42.570 --> 00:35:47.570
nor let a tear profane a moment
that's worth a martyrdom.

00:35:48.420 --> 00:35:51.330
- The virgin veil shall
guard my spotless hours,

00:35:51.330 --> 00:35:54.370
assure my peace, and
saint me for hereafter.

00:35:54.370 --> 00:35:56.100
- It cannot be.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:58.310
To Narbonne thou must bid a last adieu!

00:35:58.310 --> 00:36:01.697
And with the stranger
knight depart a bride.

00:36:01.697 --> 00:36:03.880
- Unhappy me?

00:36:03.880 --> 00:36:06.246
Too sure I have over
burthened thy charity,

00:36:06.246 --> 00:36:09.640
if thou wouldst drive me from hence,

00:36:09.640 --> 00:36:12.153
restrain thy alms, dear lady.

00:36:12.153 --> 00:36:13.678
- O Adeliza,

00:36:13.678 --> 00:36:17.953
thy words now slake and
now augment my fever!

00:36:19.050 --> 00:36:21.203
Hear my last breath.

00:36:22.400 --> 00:36:25.280
Avoid the scorpion pleasure.

00:36:25.280 --> 00:36:28.723
Death lurks beneath the velvet of his lip.

00:36:28.723 --> 00:36:31.234
O retrospect of horror.

00:36:31.234 --> 00:36:33.640
To the altar haste, Adeliza!

00:36:33.640 --> 00:36:35.720
Vow thou wilt be wretched!

00:36:35.720 --> 00:36:38.342
- Does thou then doom
me to eternal sorrows?

00:36:38.342 --> 00:36:40.210
Hast thou deceived me?

00:36:40.210 --> 00:36:41.860
- How she melts me!

00:36:41.860 --> 00:36:44.212
What have I said?

00:36:44.212 --> 00:36:47.210
Oh lovely innocence,

00:36:47.210 --> 00:36:49.250
thou art my only thought.

00:36:49.250 --> 00:36:51.820
Oh was I formed the child of sin?

00:36:51.820 --> 00:36:53.688
And I dare not embrace thee?

00:36:53.688 --> 00:36:58.510
Yet curse the hour that
stamped thee with a being!

00:36:58.510 --> 00:37:01.707
- Alas, was I then born the child of sin?

00:37:01.707 --> 00:37:03.040
Who were my parents?

00:37:03.040 --> 00:37:04.178
I will pray for them?

00:37:04.178 --> 00:37:07.441
- Oh, if the bolt must
come, let it strike me here!

00:37:07.441 --> 00:37:09.710
- Oh, raise thee from the earth.

00:37:09.710 --> 00:37:11.270
What is my lot?

00:37:11.270 --> 00:37:12.880
Wilt thou yet cherish me?

00:37:12.880 --> 00:37:16.137
- Ah, canst thou doubt
this conflict of the soul?

00:37:16.137 --> 00:37:21.137
Oh, 'tis to shield thee
from this world of sorrows

00:37:21.870 --> 00:37:25.600
that thou must flee, must wed,

00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:29.330
must never view the
towers of Narbonne more,

00:37:29.330 --> 00:37:34.330
must never know The doom
reserved for thy sad patroness.

00:37:34.723 --> 00:37:39.723
Fly, 'ere my rage forget distinction,

00:37:40.360 --> 00:37:44.110
nature and make a medley
of unheard-of crimes.

00:37:44.110 --> 00:37:46.410
Fly, ere it be too late.

00:37:46.410 --> 00:37:47.823
- Alas, she raves.

00:37:47.823 --> 00:37:49.483
I will call for help.

00:37:51.590 --> 00:37:52.423
- She's gone.

00:37:54.700 --> 00:37:59.700
That pang, great God,
was my last sacrifice.

00:38:00.230 --> 00:38:03.292
Now recollect thyself.

00:38:03.292 --> 00:38:08.110
My soul consummate the pomp of horror

00:38:08.110 --> 00:38:10.949
with tremendous coolness.

00:38:10.949 --> 00:38:15.949
'Tis fit that reason,
punish passion's crime.

00:38:16.732 --> 00:38:18.485
Reason!

00:38:18.485 --> 00:38:21.650
Alas, 'tis one of my convulsions.

00:38:21.650 --> 00:38:24.353
Down I sink, lost in eternal torment.

00:38:27.440 --> 00:38:28.830
- She is not here.

00:38:28.830 --> 00:38:30.080
Shall we not follow her?

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:31.300
- Thou knows't her not.

00:38:31.300 --> 00:38:33.715
Her transport is fictitious.

00:38:33.715 --> 00:38:35.710
- I tremble for her life.

00:38:35.710 --> 00:38:36.812
- Thou art young.

00:38:36.812 --> 00:38:39.150
I know this Countess,

00:38:39.150 --> 00:38:40.500
an arrant heretic.

00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:41.787
She scoffs the church.

00:38:41.787 --> 00:38:43.010
Her days are numbered,

00:38:43.010 --> 00:38:45.677
and thou shalt do wisely to quit her.

00:38:45.677 --> 00:38:48.710
- Alas, She bids me go.

00:38:48.710 --> 00:38:49.983
She bids me wed the stranger knight

00:38:49.983 --> 00:38:52.290
that woo'd me at our parlour.

00:38:52.290 --> 00:38:55.040
- And thou shalt take her at her word.

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:58.210
Myself with joining your hands and lo!

00:38:58.210 --> 00:39:00.400
In happy hour, who comes to meet her boon?

00:39:00.400 --> 00:39:02.020
- In tears!

00:39:02.020 --> 00:39:05.530
That cowl shall not protect
the injurious tongue,

00:39:05.530 --> 00:39:08.090
that dare insult thy innocence.

00:39:08.090 --> 00:39:11.330
- My gracious lord,
yourself and virgin coyness

00:39:11.330 --> 00:39:13.060
must be chidden.

00:39:13.060 --> 00:39:13.893
- Unriddle, priest.

00:39:13.893 --> 00:39:15.490
My soul is too impatient to wait

00:39:15.490 --> 00:39:17.783
the impertinence of flowery dialect.

00:39:18.750 --> 00:39:21.940
Dost thou consent,

00:39:21.940 --> 00:39:23.530
sweet passion of my soul?

00:39:23.530 --> 00:39:24.710
- Forebear!

00:39:24.710 --> 00:39:25.543
It must not be.

00:39:25.543 --> 00:39:28.010
Thou shalt not wed a beggar.

00:39:28.010 --> 00:39:30.220
This orphan, this abandoned wanderer,

00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:34.140
taunted with poverty,
with shameful origin.

00:39:34.140 --> 00:39:36.850
- Lovely Adeliza placed in your arms

00:39:36.850 --> 00:39:38.750
can never feel affliction.

00:39:38.750 --> 00:39:40.160
This the good Countess knows.

00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:43.003
- By my sire's soul I will not thank her.

00:39:44.500 --> 00:39:46.920
Has she dared to scorn thee,

00:39:46.920 --> 00:39:49.630
Thou beauteous excellence?

00:39:49.630 --> 00:39:52.200
In her very presence I will espouse thee.

00:39:52.200 --> 00:39:54.010
- By heaven all's lost
should they meet now.

00:39:54.010 --> 00:39:56.560
Pray be advised heaven knows

00:39:56.560 --> 00:39:59.320
how dear I tender your felicity.

00:39:59.320 --> 00:40:01.650
The chapel is a few paces hence.

00:40:01.650 --> 00:40:05.441
Arrived there, I will speedily
pronounce a few solemn words.

00:40:05.441 --> 00:40:07.940
- Well, be it so.

00:40:07.940 --> 00:40:11.770
My fair one, this holy man advises well.

00:40:11.770 --> 00:40:12.603
- Yes,

00:40:13.780 --> 00:40:16.380
heaven, to thee I fly.

00:40:16.380 --> 00:40:18.003
Thou art my only refuge.

00:40:24.550 --> 00:40:26.171
- The business is dispatched.

00:40:26.171 --> 00:40:29.330
Their hands are joined.

00:40:29.330 --> 00:40:32.840
The puling moppet
struggled with her wishes,

00:40:32.840 --> 00:40:37.150
invoked each saint to witness
her refusal nor heeded,

00:40:37.150 --> 00:40:39.080
though I swore their golden harps

00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:41.870
were tuned to greet her hymenal hours.

00:40:41.870 --> 00:40:45.370
The impetuous Count would
have forerun the rites.

00:40:45.370 --> 00:40:47.160
The maid, affrighted,

00:40:47.160 --> 00:40:49.820
at such tumultuous unaccustomed onset,

00:40:49.820 --> 00:40:52.909
sunk lifeless on the pavement.

00:40:52.909 --> 00:40:56.100
Thus am I revenged.

00:40:56.100 --> 00:40:59.030
Proud dame of Narbonne, lo!

00:40:59.030 --> 00:41:02.566
A bare-foot monk thus pays thy scorn,

00:41:02.566 --> 00:41:05.510
thus vindicates his altars.

00:41:05.510 --> 00:41:07.580
- Ah, woe of woe!

00:41:07.580 --> 00:41:09.370
Good father, haste thee in.

00:41:09.370 --> 00:41:13.000
And speak sweet words of
comfort to our mistress

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.860
her brain is much disturbed.

00:41:14.860 --> 00:41:16.500
- Goodman exorcist.

00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:18.110
Thy pains are unavailing.

00:41:18.110 --> 00:41:20.280
Her sins press her.

00:41:20.280 --> 00:41:22.660
Guilt has unhinged her reason.

00:41:22.660 --> 00:41:26.490
- She raves upon her son and
thinks he came in vision.

00:41:26.490 --> 00:41:29.050
- 'Twas no vision.

00:41:29.050 --> 00:41:30.390
- How?

00:41:30.390 --> 00:41:32.350
- He has spoken with her.

00:41:32.350 --> 00:41:33.960
- Go to, it could not be.

00:41:33.960 --> 00:41:35.600
- I tell thee, Edmund,

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:39.170
thy quondam master's
son has seen his mother.

00:41:39.170 --> 00:41:41.860
- Oh, joyous sounds!

00:41:41.860 --> 00:41:43.807
Where is my noble lord?

00:41:43.807 --> 00:41:45.307
- Here and undone.

00:41:49.980 --> 00:41:52.360
- These sixteen years has my friend Edmund

00:41:52.360 --> 00:41:54.090
pined in banishment

00:41:54.090 --> 00:41:57.770
while masses, mummings,
goblins and processions

00:41:57.770 --> 00:41:59.280
usurp'd his heritage,

00:41:59.280 --> 00:42:01.870
and made of Narbonne A
theatre of holy interludes

00:42:01.870 --> 00:42:04.043
and fainted frauds.

00:42:04.043 --> 00:42:06.315
But day darts on these spells.

00:42:06.315 --> 00:42:09.684
The enlightened age
eschews such vile deceits

00:42:09.684 --> 00:42:14.563
and truth shall do mankind,
and Edmund, justice.

00:42:16.494 --> 00:42:18.903
- I dare not shoot the gulph.

00:42:19.779 --> 00:42:21.013
Ha, Benedict

00:42:21.013 --> 00:42:23.680
thou art a priest, thy
mission should be holy.

00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:25.629
Quick, do thy work.

00:42:25.629 --> 00:42:28.545
'Tis not the wound, it is the consequence!

00:42:28.545 --> 00:42:31.300
- Split, my heart, at this sad sight.

00:42:31.300 --> 00:42:33.827
- Stand off, thou art an accomplice.

00:42:33.827 --> 00:42:37.360
Madam, it was your
morning's gracious pleasure

00:42:37.360 --> 00:42:38.954
that I should attend you.

00:42:38.954 --> 00:42:40.040
- Ha, who are thou?

00:42:40.040 --> 00:42:41.957
- Have you forgot me, lady?

00:42:41.957 --> 00:42:43.550
- Memory is full.

00:42:43.550 --> 00:42:47.943
A head distract as mine
can hold only two objects,

00:42:47.943 --> 00:42:50.643
guilt and eternity!

00:42:50.643 --> 00:42:52.600
- He is returned,

00:42:52.600 --> 00:42:54.600
your son, have you not seen him?

00:42:54.600 --> 00:42:56.270
- Would I had never!

00:42:56.270 --> 00:42:59.930
- This villainous monk has
stepped twixt you and nature.

00:42:59.930 --> 00:43:02.610
And misreported of the noblest gentleman

00:43:02.610 --> 00:43:04.565
that treads on Christian ground.

00:43:04.565 --> 00:43:06.405
Are you a mother?

00:43:06.405 --> 00:43:08.475
- Ye saints!

00:43:08.475 --> 00:43:11.340
This was the demon prompted it, avaunt!

00:43:13.830 --> 00:43:15.650
He beckons me.

00:43:15.650 --> 00:43:19.160
I will not, lies my lord

00:43:19.160 --> 00:43:20.281
wounded in the porch?

00:43:20.281 --> 00:43:23.435
I'll tear my hair and bathe his wounds.

00:43:23.435 --> 00:43:28.157
My strength, my reason
fail, darkness surrounds me!

00:43:28.157 --> 00:43:30.190
Let me die here.

00:43:30.190 --> 00:43:31.670
- This is too much for art.

00:43:31.670 --> 00:43:36.000
- No, 'tis fictitious all
'twas I inspired the horrors

00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:39.876
she has been so kind to
utter at my suggestion.

00:43:39.876 --> 00:43:44.630
Artful woman Thou subtle
emblem of thy sex,

00:43:44.630 --> 00:43:47.179
composed of madness and deceit,

00:43:47.179 --> 00:43:50.376
but since thy brain has lost its poise,

00:43:50.376 --> 00:43:54.130
I will send those shall
shake it beyond recovery

00:43:54.130 --> 00:43:56.023
of its reeling bias.

00:44:07.932 --> 00:44:10.526
- This interval is well.

00:44:10.526 --> 00:44:14.560
'tis thy last boon, tremendous Providence!

00:44:14.560 --> 00:44:19.560
And I will use it as 'twere
the elixir of descending mercy.

00:44:19.587 --> 00:44:23.120
A woman's words, a mother's woe!

00:44:23.120 --> 00:44:28.120
But honor if I believe this
garb, is thy profession.

00:44:28.410 --> 00:44:30.388
- A soldier's honor is his virtue.

00:44:30.388 --> 00:44:33.850
A soldier and his honor exist
together, and together perish.

00:44:33.850 --> 00:44:35.290
- 'Tis enough.

00:44:35.290 --> 00:44:38.388
Nor suffer the ebbing
moments more inquiry.

00:44:38.388 --> 00:44:41.673
Adeliza, my orphan shall be thine.

00:44:42.570 --> 00:44:46.660
Nay, start not, sir, your
loves are known to me.

00:44:46.660 --> 00:44:47.733
- I love Adeliza?

00:44:49.130 --> 00:44:51.780
Lady, recall thy wandering mind.

00:44:51.780 --> 00:44:55.010
Tho's the licentious
camp and rapine's holiday

00:44:55.010 --> 00:44:56.430
have been my school,

00:44:56.430 --> 00:44:58.800
deem not so reprobate my morals,

00:44:58.800 --> 00:45:01.060
that my eye would note no distance

00:45:01.060 --> 00:45:04.810
between the harlot's glance
and my friend's bride.

00:45:04.810 --> 00:45:05.830
- Thy friend?

00:45:05.830 --> 00:45:06.663
What friend?

00:45:06.663 --> 00:45:07.887
- Lord Edmund.

00:45:07.887 --> 00:45:08.940
- What of him?

00:45:08.940 --> 00:45:12.543
- Is Adeliza's lord,
her wedded bridegroom.

00:45:15.521 --> 00:45:16.521
- Confusion!

00:45:18.280 --> 00:45:21.030
Phrenzy, blast me, all ye furies.

00:45:21.967 --> 00:45:23.952
Edmund and Adeliza!

00:45:23.952 --> 00:45:24.785
When?

00:45:24.785 --> 00:45:25.642
Where?

00:45:25.642 --> 00:45:26.640
How?

00:45:26.640 --> 00:45:28.690
Edmund and Adeliza!

00:45:28.690 --> 00:45:30.836
Quick, unsay the monstrous tale.

00:45:30.836 --> 00:45:33.580
Oh, prodigy of ruin.

00:45:33.580 --> 00:45:37.480
Does my own son then
boil with fiercer fires

00:45:37.480 --> 00:45:41.457
then scorched his impious
mother's madding veins?

00:45:41.457 --> 00:45:42.290
- What means this agony?

00:45:42.290 --> 00:45:45.030
Didst thou not grant the
maiden to his wishes?

00:45:45.030 --> 00:45:48.976
- Did I not couple distinctions horrible.

00:45:48.976 --> 00:45:53.976
Plan unnatural rites to
grace my funeral pile,

00:45:54.210 --> 00:45:56.248
and meet the furies.

00:45:56.248 --> 00:45:58.055
- Amazement!

00:45:58.055 --> 00:46:00.220
Will hasten grant, ye powers,

00:46:00.220 --> 00:46:01.833
my speed be not too late!

00:46:10.230 --> 00:46:13.663
- Dear parent, look on us,
and bless your children.

00:46:17.080 --> 00:46:18.113
- My children!

00:46:19.340 --> 00:46:20.970
Horror!

00:46:20.970 --> 00:46:25.220
Horror, yes, ye are my children!

00:46:25.220 --> 00:46:30.220
Edmund loose that hand,
'tis poison to thy soul!

00:46:30.510 --> 00:46:33.660
Hell has no venom like a child's touch!

00:46:33.660 --> 00:46:36.480
Oh, agonizing thought!

00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:38.600
Who made this marriage?

00:46:38.600 --> 00:46:43.027
Whose unhallowed breath
pronounced the incestuous sounds?

00:46:44.933 --> 00:46:46.850
- Incest, good heavens!

00:46:47.987 --> 00:46:51.350
- Yes, thou devoted victim!

00:46:51.350 --> 00:46:54.770
Let thy blood curdle to stone!

00:46:54.770 --> 00:46:57.876
Perdition circumvents thee.

00:46:57.876 --> 00:47:02.080
Oh, where this monster stands!

00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:04.000
Thy mother!

00:47:04.000 --> 00:47:05.620
Mistress!

00:47:05.620 --> 00:47:10.320
Mother of thy daughter, sister, wife!

00:47:12.773 --> 00:47:15.443
The pillar of accumulated horrors!

00:47:16.280 --> 00:47:18.620
Hear and tremble!

00:47:18.620 --> 00:47:22.160
- Yes, I do tremble, though
thy words are phrenzy.

00:47:22.160 --> 00:47:24.890
So black must be the
passions that inspired it.

00:47:24.890 --> 00:47:29.526
- O Edmund, I have burst
the bond of every tie

00:47:29.526 --> 00:47:33.210
when thou shalt know the
fullness of my crimes

00:47:33.210 --> 00:47:35.880
to which this fury did involve thy youth,

00:47:35.880 --> 00:47:39.699
it will seem piety to curse me, Edmund.

00:47:39.699 --> 00:47:41.194
Oh!

00:47:41.194 --> 00:47:42.763
Impious night!

00:47:43.630 --> 00:47:46.780
Hah, Is not that my lord?

00:47:46.780 --> 00:47:49.673
He shakes the curtains
of the nuptial couch,

00:47:49.673 --> 00:47:53.622
and starts to find a son there!

00:47:53.622 --> 00:47:54.979
- Gracious heaven!

00:47:54.979 --> 00:47:57.290
Grant that these shocking
images be raving!

00:47:57.290 --> 00:47:59.430
- Sweet lady, be composed.

00:47:59.430 --> 00:48:01.578
Benedict shall discharge our vows.

00:48:01.578 --> 00:48:06.578
- For a short interval give me reason.

00:48:06.940 --> 00:48:11.940
Heaven, it must be known
the fullness of my crime.

00:48:16.610 --> 00:48:21.610
Ye know how fondly my luxurious
fancy doated upon my lord.

00:48:23.995 --> 00:48:28.995
For eighteen months, an embassy
detained him from my bed.

00:48:30.273 --> 00:48:34.037
A harbinger announced his near return.

00:48:34.037 --> 00:48:38.846
Love dressed his image
to my longing thoughts

00:48:38.846 --> 00:48:42.488
in all its warmest colors.

00:48:42.488 --> 00:48:43.753
But the morn,

00:48:45.060 --> 00:48:47.720
in which impatience
grew almost to sickness,

00:48:47.720 --> 00:48:50.020
presented him a bloody corpse before me.

00:48:50.020 --> 00:48:52.600
I raved!

00:48:52.600 --> 00:48:54.841
The storm of disappointed passions

00:48:54.841 --> 00:48:59.383
severed all my reason,
assailed all my blood.

00:49:00.527 --> 00:49:04.750
Whether too warmly
pressed, or too officious,

00:49:04.750 --> 00:49:08.360
to turn the torrent of my grief aside,

00:49:08.360 --> 00:49:11.785
Beatrice that attended me,

00:49:11.785 --> 00:49:14.984
disclosed thy suit,

00:49:14.984 --> 00:49:16.790
unhappy boy!

00:49:16.790 --> 00:49:17.623
- What is to come?

00:49:17.623 --> 00:49:20.698
Shield me, ye gracious
powers from my own thoughts.

00:49:20.698 --> 00:49:25.440
- My fancy saw thee thy father's image.

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:27.017
- Swallow the accursed sound!

00:49:27.017 --> 00:49:28.040
Nor dare to say.

00:49:28.040 --> 00:49:29.956
- Yes, thou polluted son!

00:49:29.956 --> 00:49:33.997
Grief, disappointment, opportunity,

00:49:33.997 --> 00:49:36.880
raised such a tumult in my madding blood,

00:49:36.880 --> 00:49:40.083
I took Beatrice's place.

00:49:40.964 --> 00:49:44.820
And while thy arms
twined, to thy thinking,

00:49:44.820 --> 00:49:48.730
round another's waist,
hear, hell, and tremble

00:49:48.730 --> 00:49:53.433
thou didst clasp thy mother!

00:49:53.433 --> 00:49:54.759
(screams)

00:49:54.759 --> 00:49:55.592
- Oh, execrable!

00:49:57.180 --> 00:49:59.920
- Be that swoon eternal!

00:49:59.920 --> 00:50:01.920
Nor let her know the rest.

00:50:01.920 --> 00:50:04.590
She is thy daughter,

00:50:04.590 --> 00:50:06.860
fruit of that monstrous night!

00:50:06.860 --> 00:50:07.891
- Infernal woman!

00:50:07.891 --> 00:50:10.848
My dagger must repay, a tale like this

00:50:10.848 --> 00:50:14.370
no, I must not strike.

00:50:14.370 --> 00:50:17.380
I dare not punish what you dared commit.

00:50:17.380 --> 00:50:19.654
- Oh, give me the dagger,
my arm will not recoil.

00:50:19.654 --> 00:50:21.927
Thus, Edmund, I revenge thee!

00:50:23.490 --> 00:50:24.323
- Help!

00:50:24.323 --> 00:50:25.156
Hoa, help!

00:50:26.670 --> 00:50:29.590
- Peace and conceal our shame.

00:50:29.590 --> 00:50:31.344
Quick, frame some legend.

00:50:31.344 --> 00:50:36.344
Assist the maid an accident.

00:50:36.432 --> 00:50:37.765
- Mercy, heaven!

00:50:38.613 --> 00:50:40.144
Who did this deed?

00:50:40.144 --> 00:50:41.418
- Myself.

00:50:41.418 --> 00:50:42.730
- What was the cause?

00:50:42.730 --> 00:50:45.700
- Follow me to yon gulph,
and thou shall know.

00:50:45.700 --> 00:50:48.070
I answer not to man.

00:50:48.070 --> 00:50:49.369
- Bethink thee, lady.

00:50:49.369 --> 00:50:51.903
- Thought ebbs apace.

00:50:51.903 --> 00:50:56.903
O Edmund, could a blessing
break from my lips,

00:50:57.060 --> 00:50:59.981
and not become a curse, I would.

00:50:59.981 --> 00:51:02.564
Poor Adeliza, 'tis accomplishd!

00:51:03.873 --> 00:51:06.970
- My lord, explain these horrors.

00:51:06.970 --> 00:51:08.810
Wherefore fell your mother?

00:51:08.810 --> 00:51:10.150
And why faints your wife?

00:51:10.150 --> 00:51:12.120
- My wife?

00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:14.500
Thou damning priest!

00:51:14.500 --> 00:51:16.100
I have no wife, thou knows't it.

00:51:17.030 --> 00:51:18.777
Thou gavest me indeed

00:51:19.620 --> 00:51:23.396
no, rot my tongue ere the
dread sound escape it!

00:51:23.396 --> 00:51:26.680
Bear away that hateful monk.

00:51:26.680 --> 00:51:28.113
- Who was the prophet now?

00:51:28.950 --> 00:51:29.783
Remember me!

00:51:32.292 --> 00:51:33.250
- O Florian,

00:51:33.250 --> 00:51:36.500
we must haste to where
fell war must war assumes

00:51:36.500 --> 00:51:38.002
its ugliest form.

00:51:38.002 --> 00:51:40.800
I burn to rush on death!

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:42.997
O tender friend!

00:51:42.997 --> 00:51:45.213
I must not violate thy guiltless ear!

00:51:46.314 --> 00:51:48.870
Ha, 'tis my father calls!

00:51:48.870 --> 00:51:49.847
I dare not see him!

00:51:49.847 --> 00:51:51.550
- Be composed, my lord

00:51:51.550 --> 00:51:53.407
We are all your friends.

00:51:53.407 --> 00:51:55.722
Let us comfort your gentle bride.

00:51:55.722 --> 00:51:58.383
- Forbid it, all ye powers.

00:51:59.440 --> 00:52:02.650
O Florian, bear her to the holy sisters.

00:52:02.650 --> 00:52:05.403
Say, 'twas my mother's
will she take the veil.

00:52:06.720 --> 00:52:08.970
I must never behold her.

00:52:08.970 --> 00:52:10.810
Never more review this

00:52:10.810 --> 00:52:12.693
fear of monstrous guilt.

00:52:14.230 --> 00:52:19.213
No, to the embattled foe I
will present this hated form.

00:52:20.091 --> 00:52:25.024
Welcome be the saber that
leaves no atom of it undefaced.

00:52:25.024 --> 00:52:27.691
(bells chiming)

00:52:30.576 --> 00:52:33.409
(thunder roaring)

00:52:34.502 --> 00:52:36.752
(applause)

00:52:47.476 --> 00:52:49.809
(laughter)

00:52:53.230 --> 00:52:55.850
- When did you know in
public or in private

00:52:55.850 --> 00:52:59.210
double entrendres my
strict virtue drive at.

00:52:59.210 --> 00:53:03.360
Your muses sir, I'm not more
free from ill on Mt. Parnassus

00:53:03.360 --> 00:53:05.520
or on Strawberry Hill.

00:53:05.520 --> 00:53:08.449
And though with her
repentance you may hum one,

00:53:08.449 --> 00:53:11.557
I who not play your
countess to become one.

00:53:11.557 --> 00:53:15.580
So very guilty, and so very good

00:53:15.580 --> 00:53:19.111
an angel with such errant flesh and blood

00:53:19.111 --> 00:53:22.000
such sinning, praying, preaching,

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:25.757
I'll be kissed if I don't
think she was a methodist.

00:53:25.757 --> 00:53:27.230
(laughter)

00:53:27.230 --> 00:53:30.540
Saints are the produce of a viscous age.

00:53:30.540 --> 00:53:33.840
Crimes must abound to ere
secretaries can rage.

00:53:33.840 --> 00:53:37.440
His mask no canting confessor assumes

00:53:37.440 --> 00:53:40.360
with acted zeal no flaming bigot fumes.

00:53:40.360 --> 00:53:44.580
'Til the rich harvest nods
with the swelling grain,

00:53:44.580 --> 00:53:47.959
and the sharp sickle can assure his gain.

00:53:47.959 --> 00:53:52.070
But soon shall hypocrites,
their flights deplore

00:53:52.070 --> 00:53:56.170
nor grim enthusiasts vex Britannia more.

00:53:56.170 --> 00:53:59.420
Virtue shall guard her
daughters from their arts,

00:53:59.420 --> 00:54:04.074
shine in their eyes and
blossom in their hearts.

00:54:04.074 --> 00:54:08.410
They need no lectures and fantastic tone,

00:54:08.410 --> 00:54:12.029
their lesson lives before
them on the throne.

00:54:12.029 --> 00:54:14.279
(applause)

00:54:41.264 --> 00:54:44.300
- So I have the honor to
introduce you our fabulous cast

00:54:44.300 --> 00:54:47.066
Georgina Lock as the Countess of Narbonne.

00:54:47.066 --> 00:54:49.316
(applause)

00:54:51.310 --> 00:54:53.393
Carlos Guanche as Edmund.

00:54:55.056 --> 00:54:57.306
(applause)

00:54:59.260 --> 00:55:01.629
Gilberto Saenz as Florian.

00:55:01.629 --> 00:55:04.650
(applause)

00:55:04.650 --> 00:55:06.912
Chelsea Phillips as Adeliza.

00:55:06.912 --> 00:55:09.162
(applause)

00:55:10.780 --> 00:55:13.000
Charlie Gillespie as Benedict.

00:55:13.000 --> 00:55:15.250
(applause)

00:55:17.430 --> 00:55:21.163
Justin Crisp as Friar Martin.

00:55:21.163 --> 00:55:23.413
(applause)

00:55:25.320 --> 00:55:27.851
Dale Townshend as Peter the Porter.

00:55:27.851 --> 00:55:30.101
(applause)

00:55:32.410 --> 00:55:34.594
Stephen Clarke as the servant.

00:55:34.594 --> 00:55:36.844
(applause)

00:55:38.960 --> 00:55:43.960
And David Worall who
has abridged our text.

00:55:44.897 --> 00:55:47.147
(applause)

00:55:50.861 --> 00:55:55.455
And also Jill Campbell
who has read our prologue.

00:55:55.455 --> 00:55:57.705
(applause)

00:55:59.910 --> 00:56:02.551
And finally Misty Anderson.

00:56:02.551 --> 00:56:05.884
(applause and cheering)

00:56:14.110 --> 00:56:17.340
And we're gonna do a talk
back in just a few minutes.

00:56:17.340 --> 00:56:20.080
We're gonna just do a
quick, bring us some chairs.

00:56:20.080 --> 00:56:21.300
So please stay for that.

00:56:21.300 --> 00:56:23.120
- And some of our actors will need to go

00:56:23.120 --> 00:56:25.080
hang up these very hot clothes,

00:56:25.080 --> 00:56:27.360
but they will come back
in for the discussion.

00:56:27.360 --> 00:56:30.440
And we're planning on
maybe 20 minutes in here

00:56:30.440 --> 00:56:34.110
and then we'd like you to
join us at a reception after.

00:56:34.110 --> 00:56:34.943
- Yes.

00:56:34.943 --> 00:56:35.776
- Thank you.

00:56:35.776 --> 00:56:37.986
(applause)

00:56:41.640 --> 00:56:45.160
- While the cast is getting changed,

00:56:45.160 --> 00:56:46.780
we can get started.

00:56:46.780 --> 00:56:49.670
I'm Catherine Sheehy, I'm
the Resident Dramaturg

00:56:49.670 --> 00:56:51.310
of Yale rep and I'm the chair of the

00:56:51.310 --> 00:56:53.000
Department of Dramaturgy
and Dramatic Criticism

00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:54.460
at the Yale School of Drama,

00:56:54.460 --> 00:56:58.340
and 18th century British enthusiast.

00:56:58.340 --> 00:57:01.553
I'm delighted to welcome
you here to a talk back.

00:57:03.740 --> 00:57:04.890
I'll ask you a couple of questions,

00:57:04.890 --> 00:57:06.420
and then I'll throw it open to you.

00:57:06.420 --> 00:57:09.010
So that, just because we're recording it,

00:57:09.010 --> 00:57:11.330
there are standers by with microphones.

00:57:11.330 --> 00:57:12.561
So when you're called upon,

00:57:12.561 --> 00:57:15.460
if you would just contain your enthusiasm

00:57:15.460 --> 00:57:18.480
until the microphone can
get to you, that'd be great.

00:57:18.480 --> 00:57:20.112
I wanted to read to you
just a little bit from

00:57:20.112 --> 00:57:23.950
Horace Walpoles post
script to the 1791 edition

00:57:23.950 --> 00:57:25.500
which is about 23 years

00:57:25.500 --> 00:57:27.390
after the play was originally written.

00:57:27.390 --> 00:57:29.235
From the time that I first
undertook the foregoing scenes

00:57:29.235 --> 00:57:30.613
I never flattered myself

00:57:30.613 --> 00:57:33.460
that they would be proper
to appear on the stage.

00:57:33.460 --> 00:57:36.010
The subject's so horrid that
I thought it would shock

00:57:36.010 --> 00:57:38.210
rather than give
satisfaction to the audience.

00:57:38.210 --> 00:57:40.120
Still I found it so truly tragic

00:57:40.120 --> 00:57:42.620
in the essential springs
of terror and pity

00:57:42.620 --> 00:57:43.870
that I could not resist the impulse

00:57:43.870 --> 00:57:45.470
of adapting it to the scene,

00:57:45.470 --> 00:57:48.144
but could never be practicable
to produce it there.

00:57:48.144 --> 00:57:49.161
(laughter)

00:57:49.161 --> 00:57:50.540
See.

00:57:50.540 --> 00:57:52.400
See how wrong we can be 300 years later.

00:57:52.400 --> 00:57:55.910
I saw that it would
admit of great situation

00:57:55.910 --> 00:57:56.890
of lofty characters

00:57:56.890 --> 00:57:58.820
and of those sudden and unforeseen strokes

00:57:58.820 --> 00:58:00.160
which have often singular effect

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:02.110
in operating a revolution in the passions,

00:58:02.110 --> 00:58:03.890
and in interesting the spectator.

00:58:03.890 --> 00:58:05.528
It was capable of furnishing
not only a contrast

00:58:05.528 --> 00:58:08.140
of characters, but a
contrast of virtue and vice

00:58:08.140 --> 00:58:10.613
in the same character,
sitting right there.

00:58:10.613 --> 00:58:12.070
And by laying the scene

00:58:12.070 --> 00:58:13.790
in what age and country I pleased,

00:58:13.790 --> 00:58:14.973
Catholic France,

00:58:14.973 --> 00:58:17.180
pictures of ancient manners might be drawn

00:58:17.180 --> 00:58:19.340
and many illusions to
historic events introduced

00:58:19.340 --> 00:58:22.080
to bring the action nearer the
imagination of the spectator.

00:58:22.080 --> 00:58:24.290
The moral resulting from
the calamities attended

00:58:24.290 --> 00:58:27.330
on unbounded passions, obviously
the moral of the story,

00:58:27.330 --> 00:58:29.520
even to the destruction
of the criminal's race

00:58:29.520 --> 00:58:33.060
was obviously suited to the
purpose and object of tragedy.

00:58:33.060 --> 00:58:34.616
So I thought that would be a
good place for us to start,

00:58:34.616 --> 00:58:36.489
since we have some scholars up here.

00:58:36.489 --> 00:58:40.151
I wanted to ask, is the
mysterious mother a tragedy.

00:58:40.151 --> 00:58:43.910
What is the place, purpose
and object would you say.

00:58:43.910 --> 00:58:46.060
I would be happy to
throw it out to anybody

00:58:46.060 --> 00:58:47.473
who'd like to answer.

00:58:48.860 --> 00:58:50.214
- Well, I think,

00:58:50.214 --> 00:58:54.900
there's a kind of a textual fault line

00:58:54.900 --> 00:58:57.324
in the play

00:58:57.324 --> 00:58:59.888
when we conceptualize it as a tragedy.

00:58:59.888 --> 00:59:04.470
On the one hand he mentions
aristotelian categories

00:59:04.470 --> 00:59:05.679
of pity and terror,

00:59:05.679 --> 00:59:09.370
and harking back to an aristotelian
understanding of tragedy

00:59:09.370 --> 00:59:11.161
in the post script that you've just read.

00:59:11.161 --> 00:59:14.628
But on the other hand, as the

00:59:14.628 --> 00:59:19.110
prologue to a piece makes clear

00:59:19.110 --> 00:59:21.490
he is trying to differentiate himself

00:59:21.490 --> 00:59:25.140
from classism and indeed
French neo classism

00:59:25.140 --> 00:59:26.970
of the 18th century

00:59:26.970 --> 00:59:30.377
which subscribes to
aristotelian models of tragedy

00:59:30.377 --> 00:59:34.370
and in fact holds Shakespeare responsible

00:59:34.370 --> 00:59:36.220
for deviating from those

00:59:36.220 --> 00:59:38.229
and seeing him as kind
of gothic and barbaric

00:59:38.229 --> 00:59:41.080
and uncouth and uncivilized

00:59:41.080 --> 00:59:43.050
because he doesn't conform
to notions of tragedy.

00:59:43.050 --> 00:59:47.940
So I think the place
relationship to tragedy

00:59:47.940 --> 00:59:49.672
is complex on the one hand,

00:59:49.672 --> 00:59:52.677
citing pity and terror and the well spring

00:59:52.677 --> 00:59:54.490
aristotelian categories.

00:59:54.490 --> 00:59:55.960
But on the other hand,

00:59:55.960 --> 00:59:59.060
differentiating himself
certainly from neo classical

00:59:59.060 --> 01:00:00.791
conceptualizations of tragedy.

01:00:00.791 --> 01:00:03.320
Therefore, Shakespeare serves him

01:00:03.320 --> 01:00:07.265
as the kind of guide and
the model to a tragic mode.

01:00:07.265 --> 01:00:11.274
And the play is replete
with references to Macbeth

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:14.250
to Hamlet in particular.

01:00:14.250 --> 01:00:16.147
I think those are the models

01:00:16.147 --> 01:00:18.250
to which he turns bearing in mind

01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:21.820
for the 18th century
Shakespeare is the gothic bard,

01:00:21.820 --> 01:00:24.680
gothic in a very different sense, yes.

01:00:24.680 --> 01:00:26.660
- So essentially an Englishman

01:00:26.660 --> 01:00:28.850
wanted to let us know
the French got it wrong?

01:00:28.850 --> 01:00:30.283
- Yes.
- Yup, that's very odd.

01:00:30.283 --> 01:00:32.860
- As he does in the preface to “Otranto”.

01:00:32.860 --> 01:00:35.130
- Right, well Walpole actually courted,

01:00:35.130 --> 01:00:35.970
comparisons to Shakespeare

01:00:35.970 --> 01:00:38.510
as his literary target of aspiration

01:00:38.510 --> 01:00:40.750
as Jill read in the prologue.

01:00:40.750 --> 01:00:43.100
Here he's taken that old
Shakespearian chestnut

01:00:43.100 --> 01:00:45.440
the bed trick, and he's inverted right

01:00:45.440 --> 01:00:46.860
as a seat of disaster
rather than the wake

01:00:46.860 --> 01:00:49.000
of the comic resolution
as it is in all is well

01:00:49.000 --> 01:00:51.450
and somewhat less merrily
in measure for measure.

01:00:53.320 --> 01:00:54.650
Maybe you can talk a little bit about

01:00:54.650 --> 01:00:58.040
describing the bed trick, Georgina

01:00:59.968 --> 01:01:01.710
and what kind emotions that you go through

01:01:01.710 --> 01:01:04.910
while you're imagining that old chestnut.

01:01:04.910 --> 01:01:05.743
- The bed trick.

01:01:07.460 --> 01:01:10.840
Well, I don't have a son,

01:01:10.840 --> 01:01:12.800
but I've got quite a good imagination.

01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:15.050
(laughter)

01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:21.060
I kind of like the lines
where she's moving between

01:01:22.100 --> 01:01:25.100
loving what she sees as a son

01:01:25.100 --> 01:01:26.800
and at the same time being disgusted.

01:01:26.800 --> 01:01:27.840
Loving what she sees as a husband

01:01:27.840 --> 01:01:28.673
and being disgusted by her son,

01:01:28.673 --> 01:01:32.725
which is quite an interesting
position to be in.

01:01:32.725 --> 01:01:36.890
And I suppose that it's,

01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:39.510
I mean I can't really think
of anything worse to do

01:01:39.510 --> 01:01:41.030
apart from murder.

01:01:41.030 --> 01:01:44.400
So I'm in a very difficult place really.

01:01:44.400 --> 01:01:46.610
And I also think it's
slightly weird to sleep

01:01:46.610 --> 01:01:49.110
with somebody the night
that somebody dies anyway.

01:01:50.380 --> 01:01:53.540
So I did find it quite difficult

01:01:53.540 --> 01:01:57.210
to get in to her from the inside,

01:01:57.210 --> 01:01:58.762
but the more I'd read the script,

01:01:58.762 --> 01:02:03.230
and the more I kind of read
the language of the script

01:02:03.230 --> 01:02:07.060
and the things about guilt and innocence

01:02:07.060 --> 01:02:10.414
and the rhetoric that she uses,

01:02:10.414 --> 01:02:14.370
it helped me to kind of use the script

01:02:14.370 --> 01:02:16.550
to just kind of portray
what she's going through

01:02:16.550 --> 01:02:18.541
then sometimes you start to feel it

01:02:18.541 --> 01:02:21.570
and actually what I used

01:02:21.570 --> 01:02:23.060
to try to get closer to it,

01:02:23.060 --> 01:02:26.090
I mean we talked about the spine

01:02:26.090 --> 01:02:28.820
in which it kind of keeping
the spine very straight

01:02:28.820 --> 01:02:30.400
and then bending.

01:02:30.400 --> 01:02:32.640
The idea of being disgusted by yourself,

01:02:32.640 --> 01:02:34.602
your stomach starts to kind of shrink

01:02:34.602 --> 01:02:38.780
and want to kind of vomit by
the idea of what you've done

01:02:38.780 --> 01:02:41.096
and that kind of physical clue

01:02:41.096 --> 01:02:45.111
helped me with getting closer

01:02:45.111 --> 01:02:46.797
to that

01:02:49.490 --> 01:02:51.573
well let's call it a sin, it's a sin.

01:02:51.573 --> 01:02:53.899
(laughs)

01:02:53.899 --> 01:02:55.185
- This also sort of touches on,

01:02:55.185 --> 01:02:58.500
meaning the moments of nervous
laughter as you might imagine

01:02:58.500 --> 01:03:01.663
and we only got together on
Monday night for the first time.

01:03:03.490 --> 01:03:05.639
But we sorta had to speed
through the process.

01:03:05.639 --> 01:03:08.107
And in thinking about this sort of,

01:03:08.107 --> 01:03:10.310
the horrific bed trick

01:03:10.310 --> 01:03:13.150
we're also back to your first
question in a way Catherine

01:03:13.150 --> 01:03:14.450
is this a tragedy?

01:03:14.450 --> 01:03:16.350
The over-the-topness of it

01:03:16.350 --> 01:03:17.830
which is also something that,

01:03:17.830 --> 01:03:19.570
especially for those scholars in the room

01:03:19.570 --> 01:03:22.028
who teach “Otranto” to undergraduates.

01:03:22.028 --> 01:03:25.419
Is this funny when the helmet falls right?

01:03:25.419 --> 01:03:27.210
And crushes the son.

01:03:27.210 --> 01:03:30.290
Is something absurd around the corner.

01:03:30.290 --> 01:03:33.298
So we are comparing the musical version.

01:03:33.298 --> 01:03:35.130
(laughter)

01:03:35.130 --> 01:03:37.752
We'll have lots of Mama Mia tunes.

01:03:37.752 --> 01:03:40.113
- The old tap dancing mysterious mother.

01:03:41.520 --> 01:03:43.578
Walpole said that he
never flattered himself

01:03:43.578 --> 01:03:45.830
the play would be proper
to appear on the stage

01:03:45.830 --> 01:03:47.860
and setting aside the unlikelihood

01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:49.089
that he never flattered himself,

01:03:49.089 --> 01:03:53.800
did you find the play stage
worthy for today's loosh

01:03:53.800 --> 01:03:57.985
depraved audience, like these people here.

01:03:57.985 --> 01:04:01.393
And how did you go about
making it stage worthy.

01:04:02.720 --> 01:04:04.223
- Well that's certainly David.

01:04:04.223 --> 01:04:05.475
- The thing that I did of course,

01:04:05.475 --> 01:04:07.540
because it started out as a fire back

01:04:07.540 --> 01:04:09.315
Shakespearean play,

01:04:09.315 --> 01:04:11.890
Shakespearean shape,

01:04:11.890 --> 01:04:13.580
and so I realized that you know,

01:04:13.580 --> 01:04:16.430
you wouldn't want to
stay around for two hours

01:04:16.430 --> 01:04:17.380
or something like that,

01:04:17.380 --> 01:04:19.184
so we need to get it down.

01:04:19.184 --> 01:04:21.968
So I had to cut it,

01:04:21.968 --> 01:04:23.760
which is brutal,

01:04:23.760 --> 01:04:25.855
but then I found a performance

01:04:25.855 --> 01:04:29.690
after Walpole's death

01:04:29.690 --> 01:04:32.075
where it had been performed as three acts.

01:04:32.075 --> 01:04:35.530
So I knew it could be cut,

01:04:35.530 --> 01:04:39.670
and I guess I thought probably
it should be cut as well.

01:04:39.670 --> 01:04:41.950
So that's why I did that.

01:04:41.950 --> 01:04:42.783
So I

01:04:44.230 --> 01:04:45.980
threw out things really.

01:04:45.980 --> 01:04:47.610
So what you're really doing

01:04:47.610 --> 01:04:50.040
is trying to end with the final scene.

01:04:50.040 --> 01:04:53.390
So it's a bit like landing
an aircraft to think.

01:04:53.390 --> 01:04:56.510
There's a landing strip
which is the final scene

01:04:57.920 --> 01:05:01.160
with the Countess and you
have to throw out all the

01:05:01.160 --> 01:05:04.058
luggage and the drinks, trolley,

01:05:04.058 --> 01:05:06.424
and everything in order
to be able to reach that.

01:05:06.424 --> 01:05:09.183
But an interesting thing began to happen

01:05:09.183 --> 01:05:10.617
as I worked through it.

01:05:10.617 --> 01:05:13.460
Which is that once you
throw out all the positives

01:05:13.460 --> 01:05:17.060
and you accent all the negatives

01:05:17.060 --> 01:05:19.423
like the reverse of the song,

01:05:21.647 --> 01:05:26.647
what you get then is this
kind of melodramatic line

01:05:27.460 --> 01:05:29.410
which seems to go through it.

01:05:29.410 --> 01:05:34.410
So it's kind of ideology
is freighted on this line

01:05:35.747 --> 01:05:38.429
of melodrama actually,

01:05:38.429 --> 01:05:42.250
interaction which I hope this

01:05:44.310 --> 01:05:47.559
cutting has kind of done really.

01:05:47.559 --> 01:05:51.012
And it's interesting
that it's there at all.

01:05:51.012 --> 01:05:56.012
'Cause you can see Horace
kind of making melodrama

01:05:58.585 --> 01:06:01.660
as a kind of again, a
spine going through it

01:06:01.660 --> 01:06:05.340
even though the play is
probably about other things

01:06:05.340 --> 01:06:07.840
profound things about guilt and

01:06:09.593 --> 01:06:11.790
religion and all those things,

01:06:11.790 --> 01:06:14.470
but that line seems to
go all the way through it

01:06:14.470 --> 01:06:17.720
as I kind of worked through
it and shortened it.

01:06:17.720 --> 01:06:20.460
- Yeah, and in our early conversations

01:06:20.460 --> 01:06:21.710
when you mentioned melodrama

01:06:21.710 --> 01:06:25.575
and we have a wonderful
lighting design candidate

01:06:25.575 --> 01:06:28.330
at my home University, Alice Trent,

01:06:28.330 --> 01:06:32.533
and she did these graphics for us.

01:06:34.310 --> 01:06:37.360
So that got me thinking
just about melodrama

01:06:37.360 --> 01:06:38.860
as the over the topness

01:06:38.860 --> 01:06:42.450
but also might music do some work

01:06:43.480 --> 01:06:45.930
to supply what had to be caught here.

01:06:45.930 --> 01:06:47.310
And a lot of what had to be cut,

01:06:47.310 --> 01:06:49.810
I see Charlie and Justin are back,

01:06:49.810 --> 01:06:53.860
is the religious struggle

01:06:53.860 --> 01:06:57.100
that Walpole is staging here,

01:06:57.100 --> 01:07:00.960
imagining this early reformation

01:07:00.960 --> 01:07:04.052
or almost pre-reformation
moment and coming back.

01:07:04.052 --> 01:07:07.270
So all of these zingers
about an enlightened age

01:07:07.270 --> 01:07:09.968
and reason are also in the context

01:07:09.968 --> 01:07:14.660
of a very fascinating
kind of anticlericalism

01:07:14.660 --> 01:07:17.220
that it is also a fascination

01:07:18.304 --> 01:07:22.924
with all things catholic and
a kind of pre modern past.

01:07:22.924 --> 01:07:26.980
So we were just looking
for ways to give that feel

01:07:26.980 --> 01:07:30.430
even though those debates
and the play and those lines

01:07:30.430 --> 01:07:31.710
which are very interesting

01:07:31.710 --> 01:07:33.810
might not be the most playable.

01:07:33.810 --> 01:07:36.623
- To get back to the notion
of disgust which you picked up

01:07:36.623 --> 01:07:38.680
is I think is hugely important

01:07:38.680 --> 01:07:40.067
and interesting in this play

01:07:40.067 --> 01:07:44.600
is to look at how that term for Walpole

01:07:44.600 --> 01:07:46.470
certainly in the context of this play

01:07:46.470 --> 01:07:47.690
is inseparable from

01:07:47.690 --> 01:07:51.041
a perception of female sexuality.

01:07:51.041 --> 01:07:54.000
And what seems to happen in

01:07:55.947 --> 01:07:58.660
correspondence around the play

01:07:58.660 --> 01:08:01.770
that he undertakes particularly
with this friend Mason

01:08:01.770 --> 01:08:03.470
is a concern with disgust.

01:08:03.470 --> 01:08:05.276
And it's quite clear that that disgust

01:08:05.276 --> 01:08:09.480
pertains to the fact that this is a woman

01:08:09.480 --> 01:08:13.730
who has not unconsciously
committed a tragic error

01:08:13.730 --> 01:08:17.720
but someone who desires, who is desiring,

01:08:17.720 --> 01:08:19.610
and who is a kind of sexual agent

01:08:19.610 --> 01:08:22.767
and who chooses
voluntarily and consciously

01:08:22.767 --> 01:08:24.850
her son as a bed partner.

01:08:24.850 --> 01:08:29.420
And it is that element of
disgust that Mason suggests

01:08:29.420 --> 01:08:31.216
he rewrite out of the play

01:08:31.216 --> 01:08:34.134
and turn it into an
unconscious tragic mistake.

01:08:34.134 --> 01:08:38.110
But it's quite clear that
the issue around disgust

01:08:38.110 --> 01:08:41.465
pertains to Walpole to a consciously,

01:08:41.465 --> 01:08:43.830
deliberately desiring woman,

01:08:43.830 --> 01:08:46.840
which I think he has
difficulties conceptualizing,

01:08:46.840 --> 01:08:49.396
as of course many of the
late 18th century do.

01:08:49.396 --> 01:08:52.850
- It's about that women
can't be trusted as well

01:08:52.850 --> 01:08:54.836
especially when sexually powerful

01:08:54.836 --> 01:08:56.927
the kind of last trick
that women can play.

01:08:56.927 --> 01:08:59.300
- But also, in the history of sexuality,

01:08:59.300 --> 01:09:01.629
it's only at around this
time that women are being

01:09:01.629 --> 01:09:04.165
given a sexuality of their own anyway

01:09:04.165 --> 01:09:07.030
and not seen simply as inverted

01:09:08.090 --> 01:09:10.040
desiring bodies

01:09:11.370 --> 01:09:14.300
that have sort of organs and desires

01:09:14.300 --> 01:09:17.390
that are simply inverted
versions of the masculine.

01:09:17.390 --> 01:09:19.849
But the two sex model of desiring arises

01:09:19.849 --> 01:09:21.530
in the late 18th century

01:09:21.530 --> 01:09:25.364
where women are kind of bestowed
with their own sexuality

01:09:25.364 --> 01:09:27.880
and that I think, is obviously threatening

01:09:27.880 --> 01:09:28.928
for someone like Walpole.

01:09:28.928 --> 01:09:30.720
- And these are words that Edmund uses.

01:09:30.720 --> 01:09:33.599
He calls his mother a sensual woman.

01:09:33.599 --> 01:09:36.913
And it refers to organs.

01:09:37.755 --> 01:09:39.900
I think so.

01:09:39.900 --> 01:09:40.900
- Such a play is never done

01:09:40.900 --> 01:09:43.260
until the bodies of the
women are strewn on the stage

01:09:43.260 --> 01:09:45.750
and then supremely sorry.

01:09:45.750 --> 01:09:46.743
(laughter)

01:09:46.743 --> 01:09:50.180
I think we should we open up

01:09:50.180 --> 01:09:52.500
for questions from the
audience if there are any.

01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:53.960
I mean I have some more but I don't wanna

01:09:53.960 --> 01:09:56.090
usurp your curiosity.

01:09:56.090 --> 01:09:58.354
- Oh, we do have the remainder
of the cast back in there

01:09:58.354 --> 01:09:59.187
if you have questions.

01:09:59.187 --> 01:10:00.870
- They can take questions too as well.

01:10:02.121 --> 01:10:06.942
Yes right here.

01:10:06.942 --> 01:10:10.050
- [Viewer] Well, I was
quite intrigued by this

01:10:11.643 --> 01:10:16.643
issue of female sexuality
and lust on which the

01:10:18.350 --> 01:10:20.560
whole plot turns obviously.

01:10:20.560 --> 01:10:24.040
And is this treated in

01:10:24.040 --> 01:10:26.270
other literary works at the time?

01:10:26.270 --> 01:10:29.100
Or is it treated, I
don't know, from the popehood

01:10:29.100 --> 01:10:34.100
is it treated in philosophical
writings at the time?

01:10:34.430 --> 01:10:36.997
Forgive me, I don't know much about it

01:10:36.997 --> 01:10:37.883
but it just.

01:10:39.020 --> 01:10:40.120
- Yes most definitely.

01:10:41.491 --> 01:10:43.963
- I think you can see in
Gertrude too, I mean in Hamlet.

01:10:43.963 --> 01:10:44.889
You were talking about Hamlet.

01:10:44.889 --> 01:10:49.440
The deep suspicion of a woman who,

01:10:49.440 --> 01:10:51.060
particularly a woman who has certain age

01:10:51.060 --> 01:10:52.320
who continues to desire.

01:10:52.320 --> 01:10:55.270
You've been through the
restoration with people like

01:10:55.270 --> 01:10:57.420
Mrs. Loveit in “Man of Mode”

01:10:57.420 --> 01:10:59.950
and this kind of the older woman sexuality

01:10:59.950 --> 01:11:03.520
is like a death bed for male scene.

01:11:03.520 --> 01:11:04.353
You know what I mean?

01:11:04.353 --> 01:11:05.960
And it's seen as a kind of problem.

01:11:06.881 --> 01:11:08.880
- I think that starts
in the renaissance stage

01:11:08.880 --> 01:11:10.323
on the Shakespearean stage.

01:11:11.519 --> 01:11:13.913
- In the age as well,

01:11:15.623 --> 01:11:17.839
sometime in the 1780s,

01:11:17.839 --> 01:11:21.176
there's a play called
“The Mysterious Husband,”

01:11:21.176 --> 01:11:23.540
that's about incest as well

01:11:23.540 --> 01:11:25.600
but in not quite the same way.

01:11:25.600 --> 01:11:28.330
And the storyline in that is that

01:11:31.228 --> 01:11:35.200
the English father has a mistress in Paris

01:11:35.200 --> 01:11:37.029
and then his adult son,

01:11:37.029 --> 01:11:40.570
who is estranged from
the father goes to Paris

01:11:40.570 --> 01:11:44.400
and he takes up with the mistress
unbeknownst to each other.

01:11:44.400 --> 01:11:46.930
So there's a kind of a,

01:11:46.930 --> 01:11:48.534
I guess in that period,

01:11:48.534 --> 01:11:52.340
they're exploring the limits of incest.

01:11:52.340 --> 01:11:55.003
So London audiences

01:11:55.003 --> 01:11:57.253
kind of comfortable with

01:11:57.253 --> 01:11:59.223
thinking about that I think.

01:12:00.260 --> 01:12:01.310
Perhaps they're exploring,

01:12:01.310 --> 01:12:04.895
there are probably other incest plays

01:12:04.895 --> 01:12:07.280
of the 18th century that I don't know.

01:12:07.280 --> 01:12:09.356
Dryden’s “Oedipus” for example.

01:12:09.356 --> 01:12:12.870
But this notion of the kind of dangerously

01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:15.870
desiring woman would become
a staple of gothic fiction

01:12:15.870 --> 01:12:17.410
in the late 18th century

01:12:17.410 --> 01:12:21.983
and all those invariably to
catastrophic dramatic ends.

01:12:24.800 --> 01:12:28.410
From Ann Radcliff to
Charlotte Dacre and beyond.

01:12:28.410 --> 01:12:30.170
These images of passion,

01:12:30.170 --> 01:12:32.580
the word, they become
associated with is passion

01:12:32.580 --> 01:12:34.972
which has both sentimental overtones

01:12:34.972 --> 01:12:37.307
but also sexual overtones.

01:12:37.307 --> 01:12:39.670
- And in just thinking
specifically about the stage

01:12:39.670 --> 01:12:41.790
I mean it's at the restoration

01:12:41.790 --> 01:12:44.840
that we have women playing
women's parts for the first time

01:12:44.840 --> 01:12:45.890
in English theater.

01:12:45.890 --> 01:12:48.930
And restoration comedies, those comedies

01:12:48.930 --> 01:12:51.825
between 1660 and about 1700

01:12:51.825 --> 01:12:54.090
are known for being especially

01:12:55.380 --> 01:12:57.950
sexually frank, dirty.

01:12:57.950 --> 01:13:00.010
There's lots of adultery,

01:13:00.010 --> 01:13:02.064
there's lots of sleeping around

01:13:02.064 --> 01:13:04.688
and that sort of all comes on

01:13:04.688 --> 01:13:09.136
in a burst after Charles
II reopens the theaters

01:13:09.136 --> 01:13:11.380
after the puritans had closed them.

01:13:11.380 --> 01:13:13.330
So there's a kind of cultural revenge plot

01:13:13.330 --> 01:13:15.800
on the puritans that's
going on, right, yay!

01:13:15.800 --> 01:13:17.800
The puritans are gone, we
can have sexy comedies.

01:13:17.800 --> 01:13:20.530
But also women's bodies on the stage

01:13:20.530 --> 01:13:23.850
and then that peak dies down

01:13:23.850 --> 01:13:26.430
but we still have some of those types

01:13:26.430 --> 01:13:29.760
that are part of again, discovering

01:13:29.760 --> 01:13:32.791
what the stage does when
women are embodying women.

01:13:32.791 --> 01:13:34.660
- But what is interesting too

01:13:34.660 --> 01:13:38.244
is taking the bed trick from
that bawdy tradition

01:13:38.244 --> 01:13:42.470
that comic bawdy tradition
of say William Wycherley

01:13:42.470 --> 01:13:45.070
and then repurposing it to tragic ends.

01:13:46.770 --> 01:13:48.758
- And I think too that if you think about

01:13:48.758 --> 01:13:52.450
the theater in London
was a commercial idea

01:13:52.450 --> 01:13:53.870
and the people who began to have money

01:13:53.870 --> 01:13:55.230
were of course then the merchant class,

01:13:55.230 --> 01:13:56.689
and the merchant class wanted
to see themselves on stage

01:13:56.689 --> 01:13:59.740
and then they aspired to
the toys of the aristocracy

01:13:59.740 --> 01:14:01.607
but with the morals of the bourgeoisie

01:14:01.607 --> 01:14:03.350
and so you get fetishization.

01:14:03.350 --> 01:14:05.150
And I think the sentimental
comedy goes a long way

01:14:05.150 --> 01:14:06.050
toward the gothic.

01:14:08.058 --> 01:14:08.891
Like you get the conscious lovers

01:14:08.891 --> 01:14:10.330
and then you just put it amphetamines

01:14:10.330 --> 01:14:11.714
and you get “The Mysterious Mother.”

01:14:11.714 --> 01:14:13.332
(laughter)

01:14:13.332 --> 01:14:15.240
- I like that.

01:14:15.240 --> 01:14:16.800
- Other questions?

01:14:16.800 --> 01:14:17.950
Yes, Stephen yeah.

01:14:25.226 --> 01:14:26.560
- [Viewer] Is there not a contrast

01:14:26.560 --> 01:14:30.240
between the absolute
fundamental to the disgust

01:14:30.240 --> 01:14:32.473
and fear of female sexuality

01:14:32.473 --> 01:14:35.620
which one suspects has real personal,

01:14:35.620 --> 01:14:37.853
relevance or resonance rather for Walpole.

01:14:39.360 --> 01:14:42.763
And the other main sort
of obvious theme comes out

01:14:42.763 --> 01:14:45.370
in terms of catholicism
and anticatholicism

01:14:45.370 --> 01:14:47.590
which is infinitely more layered

01:14:47.590 --> 01:14:51.032
and where he seems to be using, is a trope as it were?

01:14:51.032 --> 01:14:54.580
It's a device which uses

01:14:54.580 --> 01:14:58.980
in order to achieve dramatic effect.

01:14:58.980 --> 01:15:00.883
It's mental it's not felt.

01:15:03.440 --> 01:15:05.020
- I think that's a good question.

01:15:05.020 --> 01:15:06.610
And were Charlie Gillespie down here,

01:15:06.610 --> 01:15:07.960
I would make him answer it.

01:15:09.800 --> 01:15:12.185
Yeah, I think that that's
an important distinction

01:15:12.185 --> 01:15:13.551
whatever disgust is,

01:15:13.551 --> 01:15:18.052
particularly Walpole and
his possible sexuality

01:15:18.052 --> 01:15:21.100
in his disgust at the idea of woman

01:15:21.100 --> 01:15:25.640
and the religious debate

01:15:25.640 --> 01:15:26.890
that's playing out here.

01:15:26.890 --> 01:15:29.270
But I think the intersecting
Benedict, you know

01:15:31.190 --> 01:15:33.330
for Rome, I forgot I am a man.

01:15:33.330 --> 01:15:36.213
The kind of outsiderness

01:15:37.220 --> 01:15:40.170
to heterosexuality.

01:15:40.170 --> 01:15:41.850
- But I think the difference is that

01:15:41.850 --> 01:15:43.270
in relation to Catholicism,

01:15:43.270 --> 01:15:45.879
Walpole can never safely adopt

01:15:45.879 --> 01:15:50.100
an unequivocal attitude of disgust

01:15:50.100 --> 01:15:53.150
in the way that he can in
relation to femininity.

01:15:53.150 --> 01:15:54.720
It's much more ambivalent

01:15:54.720 --> 01:15:56.250
in relation to catholicism,

01:15:56.250 --> 01:15:58.346
not least of all because of catholicism's

01:15:58.346 --> 01:16:00.530
architectural heritage

01:16:00.530 --> 01:16:01.780
that's he's deliberately caught in

01:16:01.780 --> 01:16:03.326
at Strawberry Hill.

01:16:03.326 --> 01:16:08.326
There's a very problematic
attempt of Walpole

01:16:10.470 --> 01:16:13.660
to distinguish between the
aesthetics of catholicism

01:16:13.660 --> 01:16:16.920
and its theological legacy.

01:16:16.920 --> 01:16:21.019
So the disgust is never is as abject

01:16:21.019 --> 01:16:23.270
in relation to catholicism.

01:16:23.270 --> 01:16:25.041
- [Viewer] It's part of the [indistinct].

01:16:25.041 --> 01:16:26.026
- Oh absolutely.

01:16:26.026 --> 01:16:26.861
- Oh I would say yes,

01:16:26.861 --> 01:16:28.410
and at least at the architectural
and aesthetic level,

01:16:28.410 --> 01:16:30.010
obsessed.

01:16:30.010 --> 01:16:33.000
- But I think you can
just see also anti French

01:16:33.000 --> 01:16:36.210
as well, which is the
feeling of the period.

01:16:36.210 --> 01:16:38.450
And so you go through that as a line.

01:16:38.450 --> 01:16:41.162
And I think that was bought.

01:16:41.162 --> 01:16:43.662
It becomes explorable.

01:16:43.662 --> 01:16:47.324
And again, “The Mysterious Husband,”

01:16:47.324 --> 01:16:51.143
you know the mistress is in Paris,

01:16:52.321 --> 01:16:54.950
that kind of thing going on
in the 18th century England

01:16:54.950 --> 01:16:56.863
where the French are the enemy.

01:16:58.420 --> 01:17:00.640
- And we read the
prologue and the epilogue

01:17:00.640 --> 01:17:03.217
that Walpole wrote for his own play

01:17:03.217 --> 01:17:05.740
and the bit that I read he wrote

01:17:05.740 --> 01:17:07.850
imagining Kitty Clive doing it

01:17:07.850 --> 01:17:10.380
and then take that down
a bit methodist as well.

01:17:10.380 --> 01:17:12.430
So I said, of course I have to take this.

01:17:13.450 --> 01:17:15.260
I think that they are again,

01:17:15.260 --> 01:17:16.716
we're coming back to

01:17:16.716 --> 01:17:18.630
the religious context

01:17:18.630 --> 01:17:19.660
and we can't undersell that.

01:17:19.660 --> 01:17:21.010
Even if we had to leave some of that

01:17:21.010 --> 01:17:22.380
on the cutting room floor

01:17:22.380 --> 01:17:25.413
to get this play in this space.

01:17:25.413 --> 01:17:26.330
- Yes, yes.

01:17:27.663 --> 01:17:28.676
- [Viewer] How did you get together

01:17:28.676 --> 01:17:31.077
a cast from so many different places?

01:17:31.077 --> 01:17:32.843
(laughter)

01:17:32.843 --> 01:17:34.010
- Persistence.

01:17:35.730 --> 01:17:37.010
We planned ahead

01:17:37.010 --> 01:17:40.550
and I twisted arms in many cases,

01:17:40.550 --> 01:17:42.177
and Cindy Roman too,

01:17:42.177 --> 01:17:43.880
and we put our heads together

01:17:43.880 --> 01:17:45.650
and thought about people
who have connection

01:17:45.650 --> 01:17:47.089
to the Lewis Walpole Library

01:17:47.089 --> 01:17:50.791
and people who might
be available and around

01:17:50.791 --> 01:17:53.740
for which they were so
generous with their time.

01:17:53.740 --> 01:17:56.388
Joe Roach helped me find those fantastic

01:17:56.388 --> 01:17:58.462
young men, and Carlos is here,

01:17:58.462 --> 01:18:01.010
and Gilberto had to go.

01:18:01.010 --> 01:18:04.820
So we wove it together and we did truly,

01:18:04.820 --> 01:18:07.443
just get together for the
first time on Monday night.

01:18:08.393 --> 01:18:10.640
- And one more question, yes right here.

01:18:13.410 --> 01:18:14.643
- [Viewer] Thank you.

01:18:14.643 --> 01:18:16.863
I noticed that the
actress who played Adeliza

01:18:16.863 --> 01:18:18.883
is quite the high maiden.

01:18:18.883 --> 01:18:20.617
(laughter)

01:18:20.617 --> 01:18:22.582
And I wanted to ask a question with her.

01:18:22.582 --> 01:18:27.170
Walpole was most unhappy
with Adeliza, wasn't he?

01:18:27.170 --> 01:18:29.260
He did say, that he was not so happy,

01:18:29.260 --> 01:18:30.793
he really loved the play

01:18:30.793 --> 01:18:34.048
but he did say that the character
hadn't come up quite right

01:18:34.048 --> 01:18:37.114
and it's really very interesting to do

01:18:37.114 --> 01:18:39.680
(laughter)

01:18:39.680 --> 01:18:40.977
doing so little.

01:18:46.468 --> 01:18:49.146
- [Chelsea] Can everybody hear
me if I don't use the mic.

01:18:49.146 --> 01:18:50.865
- Use the mic.

01:18:50.865 --> 01:18:52.415
- [Chelsea] Oh sorry.

01:18:52.415 --> 01:18:56.880
It is a bit hard, and in
part because of the wonderful

01:18:56.880 --> 01:18:58.010
cutting that David gave us,

01:18:58.010 --> 01:18:59.993
which is very playable.

01:19:02.593 --> 01:19:04.710
I sort of have this
pattern where I come on

01:19:04.710 --> 01:19:06.220
and I kneel and I cry

01:19:07.120 --> 01:19:08.930
and then I leave.

01:19:08.930 --> 01:19:13.930
And use what's happening
on stage around me.

01:19:14.120 --> 01:19:15.700
So sure, there isn't a lot to do

01:19:15.700 --> 01:19:18.940
but actually as I was able to watch us

01:19:18.940 --> 01:19:21.820
sort of move through the
whole arch of the story

01:19:21.820 --> 01:19:23.040
over the last couple of days,

01:19:23.040 --> 01:19:25.070
I started to realize more and more.

01:19:25.070 --> 01:19:27.100
And I think there is
something very relatable

01:19:27.100 --> 01:19:28.560
about the fact that

01:19:28.560 --> 01:19:31.487
Adeliza is so dependent on the Countess

01:19:31.487 --> 01:19:34.060
with sort of everything in her life,

01:19:34.060 --> 01:19:36.830
including all of her sort
of emotional well being.

01:19:36.830 --> 01:19:39.167
And so when the countess
starts to break down,

01:19:39.167 --> 01:19:41.880
I think there seems to
be a lot of inconsistency

01:19:41.880 --> 01:19:43.810
in Adeliza, is she excited
about being married?

01:19:43.810 --> 01:19:44.960
Does she not wanna get married?

01:19:44.960 --> 01:19:46.560
Does she wanna be from a nun?

01:19:46.560 --> 01:19:49.380
Does she like this mysterious
young man that she's met.

01:19:49.380 --> 01:19:50.393
It's unclear, but I think

01:19:50.393 --> 01:19:52.270
what it ultimately comes down to

01:19:52.270 --> 01:19:54.816
is that she wants to please the Countess.

01:19:54.816 --> 01:19:56.445
And so whatever the
Countess is telling her,

01:19:56.445 --> 01:20:00.228
including dooming yourself
by getting married,

01:20:00.228 --> 01:20:04.113
she's gonna say, "Okay, I'll do that."

01:20:05.310 --> 01:20:07.670
- Again, to mention the conscious lovers,

01:20:07.670 --> 01:20:09.361
again you're gonna think of Indiana.

01:20:09.361 --> 01:20:11.639
The orphan who is revealed

01:20:11.639 --> 01:20:15.389
to have either the key to
happiness or the key to ruin

01:20:15.389 --> 01:20:19.756
in the play.

01:20:19.756 --> 01:20:23.050
I think, we wanna release
you to the reception

01:20:23.050 --> 01:20:24.380
and the wine and the cheese,

01:20:24.380 --> 01:20:26.250
and congratulating the actors

01:20:26.250 --> 01:20:27.390
as you encounter them in the room,

01:20:27.390 --> 01:20:29.579
but thank you very much for staying.

01:20:29.579 --> 01:20:31.829
(applause)

01:20:39.335 --> 01:20:42.002
(angelic music)

01:21:21.173 --> 01:21:23.756
(light music)

